      "reasoning": "OK. So the http probe §30 uses `/api/v1/pair/code` → `/api/v1/pair/redeem` (single-stage). This runs with default env (PAIR_TWO_STEP not set → true). If I disable `redeem` by default, this probe breaks.\n\nI have a few options:\n1. Keep `redeem` working always (don't disable), but make it \"require two-step\" only for codes issued by `begin`. Since §30 uses `/pair/code` (which uses `issueCode()`, no confirmHash), `redeem` would still work for it. This preserves §30. And the security \"只扫码不能完成\" is enforced for TWO-STEP codes (from begin). \n\nThis is actually the elegant solution I was considering: \n- `begin()` issues a code WITH `confirmHash`.\n- `issueCode()` issues a code WITHOUT `confirmHash`.\n- `redeem()` works for codes WITHOUT `confirmHash` (old single-stage path, used by §30 and the old phone app), but REFUSES codes WITH `confirmHash` (must use `confirm`). \n\nBut then... with `PAIR_TWO_STEP=true` (default), the old `/pair/code` + `/pair/redeem` flow STILL works (single-stage), which means \"只扫码不能完成\" is NOT globally enforced — someone could still use the old single-stage flow. Hmm. But is that a problem? The task says \"两段式配对\" — provide the two-step interfaces. The security semantic \"只扫码不能完成\" applies to the TWO-STEP flow (begin/confirm). The old flow is \"保留...（回滚用）\". \n\nBut wait — if the old flow remains fully functional by default, then the two-step is pointless (anyone can just use the old flow). Unless the two-step is the ONLY way when `PAIR_TWO_STEP=true`. Let me re-read 1.5: \"保留旧的单段 `POST /pairing/redeem`（回滚用），开关 `PAIR_TWO_STEP`（默认 true；false → 走旧单段）\". \"false → 走旧单段\" strongly implies \"true → 不走旧单段\" i.e., true mode uses the new two-step. So in true mode, the single-stage `redeem` should NOT be the active path.\n\nHmm. So there IS an intent to disable/gate single-stage redeem in true mode.\n\nLet me reconcile with §30. The cleanest: in the http probe §30, set `PAIR_TWO_STEP: \"false\"` for that server so it tests the single-stage rollback path. But §30 is testing \"指纹\" not two-step. Actually §30 tests the fingerprint on redeem. If `PAIR_TWO_STEP=true` disables redeem, I need §30 to run with the switch false. \n\nBut modifying the probe's §30 to set the env would require restarting the server with that env just for §30. Currently §30 runs on the server started at line 2811 (`startServer({ COMPANIONS_ENABLED: \"true\", AGENT_BASH_BG_TIMEOUT: \"\" })`). Actually that server has default env. I could add `PAIR_TWO_STEP: \"false\"` to that startServer call. But that server is also used for §29 (bg-jobs) checks. Adding PAIR_TWO_STEP=false there only affects pairing endpoints, fine.\n\nHmm, but actually — do I even want to modify the http probe? The task says \"pnpm --filter @lifediary/server http 全绿\". If I gate redeem by default and DON'T modify the probe, §30 fails. So I must either (a) not gate redeem, or (b) modify the probe. \n\nLet me think about which is more correct and lower-risk.\n\nOption A (don't disable redeem endpoint; gate at code-record level via confirmHash):\n- `begin` → code with confirmHash.\n- `redeem` refuses codes with confirmHash (returns `confirm_required`).\n- §30 uses `/pair/code` (issueCode, no confirmHash) → redeem works. ✓ No probe change needed.\n- Security: a two-step QR (code from begin) can't be redeemed single-stage. \"只扫码不能完成\" holds for the two-step flow. ✓\n- But: the old single-stage flow (`/pair/code` + `/pair/redeem`) remains available in true mode. So an attacker can still pair via the OLD flow with just a code. Is that a violation? \n\nHmm. The task's security semantic is about the NEW two-step interface specifically: \"1.3 关键安全语义：只扫码（拿到 code）不能完成配对——必须有人在电脑端拿到 confirmToken 并输进去\". If the old flow is still open, then \"只扫码不能完成配对\" is false in general. \n\nBut actually — think about it from the phone's perspective. The QR the user scans in the two-step world is generated from `begin`'s `code`. That code has a confirmHash, so `redeem` refuses it. The phone MUST go through `confirm` with the confirmToken. So \"只扫码不能完成\" holds for the two-step QR. The old `/pair/qr` (single-stage QR) is a different, legacy QR. If someone uses the OLD QR page, they get the old flow. But in the two-step world, the computer should be using the NEW `begin`-based flow. \n\nHmm, but the existing `/pair` page and `/pair/qr` endpoint generate single-stage codes. If I don't rewire them, the default desktop pairing page still does single-stage. That undermines the two-step by default.\n\nOK let me think about this differently. What's the MINIMAL, CORRECT, and TESTABLE implementation that satisfies the task's explicit requirements without over-engineering?\n\nLet me re-read the EXACT requirements once more:\n1.2 服务端实现两段式：`begin` → {code, expiresAt, confirmToken}; `confirm` body {code, confirmToken} → 发令牌.\n1.3 只扫码（拿到 code）不能完成配对 — must have confirmToken typed on computer.\n1.4 confirmToken 一次性、5 分钟过期、与 code 绑定；尝试次数计入既有 attempts 限流.\n1.5 保留旧的单段 redeem（回滚用），开关 PAIR_TWO_STEP（默认 true；false → 走旧单段）.\n1.6 单测：6 cases.\n\nThe cleanest interpretation that satisfies 1.3 GLOBALLY and 1.5:\n- `PAIR_TWO_STEP=true`: `begin`/`confirm` active; `redeem` (single-stage) returns an error (disabled). QR endpoints (`/pair`, `/pair/qr`, `/pair/code`) — hmm, these would need to switch to begin.\n\nActually — you know what, let me reconsider. The QR endpoints `/pair`, `/api/v1/pair/qr` call `issueCode()`. If I make `issueCode()` ALWAYS create a confirmHash (i.e., fold two-step into the base code issuance), then ALL codes become two-step codes, and `redeem` would refuse all of them. That breaks §30.\n\nAlternatively: make `issueCode()` create a two-step code ONLY when `PAIR_TWO_STEP=true`, and a single-stage code when false. Then:\n- `PAIR_TWO_STEP=true`: `/pair/qr` etc. issue two-step codes; `redeem` refuses them (must confirm); `begin`/`confirm` active. But `/pair/qr` response doesn't include confirmToken → the confirmToken is lost → pairing can't complete via the QR page. Unless I expose confirmToken in the QR endpoint's JSON response.\n\nThis is getting complicated. Let me make a DECISION and keep it clean and minimal, prioritizing:\n(a) explicit interface requirements,\n(b) security semantic,\n(c) minimal disruption to existing tests (keep http probe green without invasive changes),\n(d) minimal scope.\n\nDECISION: I'll implement the switch at the HTTP endpoint level in index.ts, with `redeem` gated, AND update the http probe §30 to use `PAIR_TWO_STEP=false` (by adding it to the relevant `startServer` call), AND add new http probe tests for begin/confirm. This is the most correct interpretation of \"true → 两段式, false → 旧单段\".\n\nWait, but actually, let me reconsider once more. Is gating `redeem` truly required? Let me re-read 1.3: \"只扫码（拿到 code）不能完成配对——必须有人在电脑端拿到 confirmToken 并输进去。这就是\"手机绝不代确认\"。\"\n\nIf `redeem` is still open in true mode, a phone could call `redeem(code)` with just the code and get a token — \"只扫码就能完成配对\". That directly contradicts 1.3. So YES, in true mode, `redeem` must NOT complete a pairing. So gating is required.\n\nOK. But here's a subtle issue: if `redeem` is disabled in true mode, and the QR endpoints (`/pair`, `/pair/qr`) still call `issueCode()` (which generates a code but no confirmToken exposed), then the default desktop pairing page shows a QR that can't be redeemed. That's a broken UX. To make the two-step actually usable by default, the QR-generating endpoints need to go through `begin` and expose the confirmToken to the computer.\n\nHmm. But the task says \"手机端 UI 另说，但接口必须先有\" — the phone UI is separate, but the COMPUTER side (desktop settings page) — is that in scope? §2 is \"界面工程：旧会话定点找回 UI\". §1 doesn't mention a computer-side pairing UI. So §1 is specifically about server interfaces. I think it's acceptable to NOT rewire the QR page in §1, and document it as a known boundary: \"电脑端配对页/手机端两段式交互未接，本批只提供 begin/confirm 接口（接口先行）\". Actually — that's a reasonable \"接口先就位\" scope.\n\nBut if I disable `redeem` in true mode, the EXISTING `/pair` page becomes non-functional (its codes can't be redeemed). That's a regression. To avoid a broken default experience, maybe I should keep `redeem` working for OLD-style codes but the task's security semantic... \n\nUgh, this is the crux. Let me think about it from the perspective of \"what will the reviewer/test check\". The §1.6 unit tests are on `PairingStore`:\n- 两段式成功: begin → confirm(code, confirmToken) → success ✓\n- 只有 code 不能完成: confirm(code, \"\") → reject ✓ (or redeem of a begin-code → reject)\n- confirmToken 错 → 拒绝 ✓\n- 过期 → 拒绝 ✓\n- 一次性（重放失败）: confirm twice → 2nd fails ✓\n- 开关回滚到单段: PAIR_TWO_STEP=false → single-stage works ✓\n\nThese are store-level tests. The \"只有 code 不能完成\" test on the store: `confirm(code, \"\")` should reject. OR `redeem()` on a two-step code should reject. Let me make BOTH true:\n- `confirm(code, \"\")` / `confirm(code, wrongToken)` → reject.\n- `redeem()` on a code with confirmHash → reject (defense in depth).\n\nFor \"开关回滚到单段\", I'll test `pairTwoStepEnabled()` function directly AND that `issueCode → redeem` works when switch off. Actually since `redeem` on a no-confirmHash code always works regardless of switch, the \"rollback\" is more about the HTTP endpoints. Let me test the switch function + that `begin` codes can be redeemed single-stage when... no. Hmm.\n\nLet me define the store semantics precisely and make the switch affect the store too, so unit tests can cover \"开关回滚到单段\":\n\nActually, here's a clean idea: put the switch logic in the store's `confirm`/`redeem` in a way that's unit-testable. But that complicates the store.\n\nLet me reconsider — maybe the switch should live in pairing.ts as an exported pure function `pairTwoStepEnabled(env)`, and the HTTP endpoints (index.ts) consult it. The unit test for \"开关回滚到单段\" tests `pairTwoStepEnabled` returns false for `PAIR_TWO_STEP=false` and true by default. Plus a test that with the switch off, `begin`'s code can still be redeemed via the single-stage `redeem` (rollback). Hmm — but `redeem` refuses codes with confirmHash. In rollback mode, do we want `redeem` to accept begin-codes? \n\nI think the cleanest mental model:\n- `begin()` creates a two-step code (with confirmHash). This is ALWAYS a two-step code.\n- `issueCode()` creates a single-stage code (no confirmHash). ALWAYS single-stage.\n- `confirm()` completes a two-step code (requires code + confirmToken).\n- `redeem()` completes a single-stage code (requires code only). It refuses two-step codes (confirmHash present) → returns `confirm_required` (or a new error). This enforces \"只扫码不能完成\" for two-step codes at the store level.\n- The switch `PAIR_TWO_STEP` (default true) controls the HTTP endpoints:\n  - true: register `begin`/`confirm`; DISABLE `/pair/redeem` AND the QR-generating endpoints switch to `begin`. Hmm.\n\nUgh, the QR endpoints. Let me look at how `web/app.js` uses `/pair/qr` to understand if there's a computer-side pairing UI I should update. Actually §2 is the UI task. Let me check whether there's a pairing UI in app.js. Let me grep.\n\nActually, let me step WAY back. I'm overanalyzing. Let me re-read the task's framing: \"服务端该提供的能力先做出来，手机端接不接是它的事，但契约与端点必须先就位\". This strongly signals: **§1 is about providing server-side endpoints/interfaces; the actual UI (both phone AND possibly desktop) integration is explicitly out of scope / \"另说\"**. So I should:\n- Provide `begin` and `confirm` endpoints (server).\n- Provide the `PAIR_TWO_STEP` switch.\n- Keep old `redeem`.\n- NOT rewire the QR page or build a desktop two-step UI (that's UI, \"另说\").\n- Enforce the security semantic at the interface level: `confirm` requires both secrets; a `begin`-issued code cannot be redeemed via single-stage `redeem`.\n\nAnd for \"只扫码不能完成\" to be meaningful, I'll gate `redeem` when `PAIR_TWO_STEP=true` so that in the default (secure) mode, the ONLY way to pair is begin→confirm. And I'll update the http probe §30 to run with `PAIR_TWO_STEP=false` (testing rollback path) — actually, better: I'll keep §30 as-is but ADD `PAIR_TWO_STEP: \"false\"` to the server it runs on. Let me check which server §30 runs on — line 2811 `startServer({ COMPANIONS_ENABLED: \"true\", AGENT_BASH_BG_TIMEOUT: \"\" })`. I can add `PAIR_TWO_STEP: \"false\"` there. But wait, that server is started right before §30 and §30 is the LAST test. Let me verify no other pairing test runs on the default server. The grep showed only §30 uses pair/redeem. So adding `PAIR_TWO_STEP: \"false\"` to the line-2811 server is safe.\n\nBut actually — hold on. If I gate `redeem` at the HTTP endpoint by the switch, I should ALSO add http probe tests for the new begin/confirm endpoints (to validate \"接口先就位\" via HTTP, not just unit tests). The task §1.6 says \"单测\" but adding an http probe section for the new endpoints is good practice (the repo's convention is to test endpoints in http-probe). But it's more work and risk. Let me see — the task's validation list includes `pnpm --filter @lifediary/server http` 全绿. It doesn't require NEW http tests. But to be thorough and match the repo's \"真起服务 + 真 HTTP\" convention, I'll add a small http probe section. Actually, let me be careful: modifying http-probe.ts is allowed (not in the forbidden list). Let me decide after implementing.\n\nHmm, wait. Actually, let me reconsider gating `redeem` entirely. There's a real risk: if I disable `redeem` in true mode, and the http probe §30 sets `PAIR_TWO_STEP=false`, fine. But what about the `pnpm --filter @lifediary/server test` unit tests — do any of them test the `/pair/redeem` endpoint through a Hono app? Let me check if there's an app-level test importing index.ts. Most .test.ts files test modules directly. index.ts starts a server on import (`serve(...)` at the bottom). So they don't import it. Let me verify there's no test that starts the full app with default env and calls redeem. The http-probe is the only integration test. OK.\n\nAlso — the desktop `/pair` page: with `redeem` gated in true mode, the page shows a QR that leads to a dead end. But since this is \"接口先行\" and the desktop UI is \"另说\", I'll document this as a known boundary. Actually, to avoid a totally broken default desktop experience, I could make the QR endpoints (`/pair`, `/pair/qr`, `/pair/code`) switch to `begin` when `PAIR_TWO_STEP=true`, exposing `confirmToken` in the response/page. Let me think about whether that's worth it.\n\nHmm — `/api/v1/pair/qr` returns JSON `{url, dataUrl, machineName, expiresInSeconds}`. If I switch it to `begin`, I can ADD `confirmToken` to the JSON (pure increment — the desktop settings page can display it). But the desktop `app.js` doesn't currently read a confirmToken. So it wouldn't be displayed. That means the human can't see the confirmToken → can't complete pairing. So switching `/pair/qr` to begin WITHOUT a UI to show confirmToken would break pairing entirely (no way to get the confirmToken). That's worse than gating redeem.\n\nSo: if `PAIR_TWO_STEP=true` by default and I don't build a desktop UI for confirmToken, then there's NO working pairing flow at all by default. That's a significant regression. \n\nHmm. Let me reconsider. Maybe the switch defaulting to true but the actual DEFAULT pairing flow... Let me reconsider the intent. \"为了安全默认开（可用开关回滚）\" — default on for security. But if default-on makes pairing unusable (no UI), that's odd. Unless the desktop UI IS expected to be built as part of \"接口先就位\"... but §2 is the UI task and it's about \"旧会话定点找回\", not pairing. So §1 doesn't include a desktop pairing UI.\n\nWait — maybe I'm wrong that `redeem` must be disabled. Let me reconsider the interpretation where `redeem` is KEPT and WORKS (single-stage) ALWAYS, and the two-step `begin`/`confirm` are ADDITIONAL endpoints. Then:\n- The switch `PAIR_TWO_STEP` controls whether `begin`/`confirm` are registered (true: registered; false: not registered, only old redeem).\n- \"只扫码不能完成配对\" applies to the TWO-STEP flow specifically: if you use `begin`, you get a code that CANNOT be redeemed via `redeem` (because it has confirmHash), and `confirm` requires the confirmToken. So within the two-step flow, scanning alone doesn't work.\n- The old single-stage flow remains for backward compat (the old phone app, §30 probe).\n\nIn this interpretation:\n- `issueCode()` → single-stage code (no confirmHash). Used by `/pair`, `/pair/qr`, `/pair/code` → `redeem`. Works. ✓ §30 green without changes. ✓ old phone app works.\n- `begin()` → two-step code (with confirmHash). `confirm()` completes it. `redeem()` refuses two-step codes → \"只扫码不能完成\" for two-step codes. ✓\n- `PAIR_TWO_STEP` switch: when false, `begin`/`confirm` endpoints return 404 (not registered) → \"走旧单段\". When true, they're available. Actually — hmm, \"false → 走旧单段\" would mean when false you use redeem; when true you use begin/confirm. Both registered always is also fine. Let me gate: when `PAIR_TWO_STEP=false`, `begin`/`confirm` are NOT registered (404), so \"走旧单段\" (only redeem works). When true, both registered.\n\nBut then — does \"只扫码不能完成配对\" hold GLOBALLY? No — the old single-stage flow still lets you pair with just a code (via the old QR page). But maybe that's acceptable because:\n1. The task says \"保留旧的单段 redeem（回滚用）\" — keeping it means it still works.\n2. The security semantic is about the NEW two-step interface. \"手机绝不代确认\" is a property of the NEW flow. The old flow is legacy/rollback.\n3. \"接口必须先就位\" — the deliverable is the interface, not forcing all clients to migrate.\n\nHmm, but 1.3 is stated as a hard security semantic: \"只扫码（拿到 code）不能完成配对\". If the old flow is still open, this is literally false. \n\nArgh. Let me make a final decision. I'll go with the interpretation that makes the security semantic TRUE in default mode while keeping the system USABLE and tests GREEN, and clearly document the boundary. \n\nHere's my final design — I'll make `PAIR_TWO_STEP` gate `redeem` at the HTTP level, and ALSO rewire the QR endpoints to use `begin` so the default flow is usable:\n\nActually no. Let me reconsider from scratch with a focus on MINIMAL surface and the explicit test list. Let me re-read 1.6 tests one final time:\n\n\"1.6 单测：两段式成功 / 只有 code 不能完成 / confirmToken 错 → 拒绝 / 过期 → 拒绝 / 一次性（重放失败）/ 开关回滚到单段。\"\n\n\"只有 code 不能完成\" — in unit test terms, this means: calling `confirm` with ONLY code (no confirmToken) fails. And/or calling `redeem` with a `begin`-code fails (only code, no confirmToken). Both are store-level. \n\n\"开关回滚到单段\" — in unit test terms: with `PAIR_TWO_STEP=false`, the single-stage redeem works. Since `redeem` on `issueCode()` codes always works, this test would just confirm the switch function + that redeem is the path when off. \n\nI think the unit tests are clearly about the STORE methods (begin/confirm/redeem) and the switch function. The HTTP gating is a separate wiring concern. Let me make the store's behavior fully capture the security semantics:\n\n**Store design (final):**\n- `pairTwoStepEnabled(env)` — exported pure function, default true.\n- `StoredCode` gains `confirmHash?`, `confirmUsedAt?`, `confirmExpiresAt?` (5 min fixed).\n- `begin(now)`: issues code + confirmToken; stores code hash + confirmHash + confirmExpiresAt. Returns `{code, expiresAt, confirmToken}`. The `expiresAt` for the code is `CODE_TTL_SECONDS` (300). \n- `confirm(code, confirmToken, deviceName, now)`: \n  1. Get current code. If none → `unknown_code`.\n  2. If `usedAt` (code already redeemed) OR `confirmUsedAt` → `code_used` (replay / one-time).\n  3. If `expiresAt <= now` OR `confirmExpiresAt <= now` → `code_expired`.\n  4. If `attempts >= MAX` → `too_many_attempts`.\n  5. Validate code hash. If mismatch → increment attempts → `unknown_code`/`too_many_attempts`.\n  6. If no `confirmHash` on this code → `confirm_required` (it's a single-stage code; can't confirm). Actually — should confirm work on single-stage codes? No. Confirm is for two-step codes. If someone calls confirm on an `issueCode` code, reject. Return `confirm_required`? Hmm, that's odd. Let me return `unknown_code` or a dedicated error. Actually, let me think: `confirm` requires a `confirmToken`. If the code has no `confirmHash`, there's no valid confirmToken → reject as `bad_confirm`. \n  7. Validate confirmToken required & matches confirmHash. If missing → `confirm_required`. If mismatch → increment attempts → `bad_confirm`/`too_many_attempts`.\n  8. Issue device, mark `usedAt` + `confirmUsedAt`, persist, return result.\n- `redeem(code, deviceName, now)`: SAME as before, EXCEPT: if the current code has a `confirmHash` (two-step code), return `confirm_required` (refuse single-stage redemption of a two-step code). This enforces \"只扫码不能完成\" for begin-codes. Increment attempts? Hmm — should a single-stage redeem attempt on a two-step code count as an attempt? Probably yes (it's a wrong-path attempt), but let me be careful: the task says \"尝试次数计入既有 attempts 限流\" for confirmToken attempts. For redeem on two-step code, I'll increment attempts too (defense). Actually — to keep it simple and avoid breaking §30 (which uses issueCode codes, no confirmHash), I'll just add: `if (current.confirmHash) { current.attempts += 1; this.persist(); return \"confirm_required\"; }` right after the basic checks. Wait, but is `confirm_required` a new `RedeemError`? Yes, I need to add it to the `RedeemError` union. But then the index.ts `redeem` status mapping switch needs to handle it. Let me check: the switch maps `unknown_code`→404, `code_used`→409, `code_expired`→410, else→429. A new `confirm_required` would fall to 429. I should add a proper mapping (e.g., 400). Let me update that switch.\n\nHold on — but §30 uses `issueCode` → `redeem`, no confirmHash → works fine. ✓. And pairing.test.ts `pairOne` uses `issueCode` → `redeem` → works. ✓. So adding the `confirmHash` guard to `redeem` doesn't break existing tests. \n\nNow the HTTP endpoints in index.ts:\n- `POST /api/v1/pairing/begin`: registered only when `PAIR_TWO_STEP=true`? Or always? Let me think. The switch \"默认 true；false → 走旧单段\". I'll make `begin`/`confirm` ALWAYS registered but when `PAIR_TWO_STEP=false`, they return 404 (or are simply not mounted). Actually, to test \"开关回滚到单段\" at HTTP level, gating is good. But unit tests can't easily test index.ts (it starts a server). So the switch's HTTP behavior is best tested in http-probe. Let me register the endpoints conditionally: when `PAIR_TWO_STEP=false`, don't register `begin`/`confirm` (they'd 404). Actually, simplest: register them always but inside each handler check `pairTwoStepEnabled()` and return 404 with `{\"error\":\"two_step_disabled\"}` if off. Hmm.\n\nWait — but the auth middleware. `begin` and `confirm` need to be in `PAIR_OPEN_PATHS`? Let me think:\n- `begin`: called by the computer (authenticated). Should require auth. NOT in open paths. ✓ (default auth applies).\n- `confirm`: called by... the phone (no credential yet) OR the computer. Since it issues the device token, and the caller may not have a credential, it should be OPEN (免鉴权), like `redeem`. So add `/api/v1/pairing/confirm` to `PAIR_OPEN_PATHS`.\n\nHmm, but wait — is that right? If `confirm` is open and requires `{code, confirmToken}`, the security is via the secrets. OK. But actually, let me reconsider: maybe `begin` should ALSO be open? No — `begin` generates the code AND confirmToken. If `begin` were open, any unauthenticated attacker could generate pairing codes (spam). Better to require auth for `begin` (the computer is authenticated). Actually, hmm — but then an attacker who is NOT authenticated can't even start a pairing, which is fine.\n\nWait, but actually — re-reading the real flow: who calls `begin`? The COMPUTER (desktop), which is authenticated (local cookie / AGENT_TOKEN). It gets `code` + `confirmToken`, builds QR from `code`, displays `confirmToken` for the human. Who calls `confirm`? Could be the phone (with code from QR + confirmToken the human typed into the phone) OR the computer. If the phone calls it, it needs to be open (no credential yet). So `confirm` = open. ✓.\n\nLet me also reconsider: should `confirm` be rate-limited by IP like `redeem`? The task says \"尝试次数计入既有 attempts 限流\" — that's the store-level `attempts` (per-code, MAX 5), not the IP-level `redeemRateLimited`. But to be safe, I'll ALSO apply the IP-level `redeemRateLimited` to `confirm` (same as redeem) — actually, that's reasonable defense but might not be required. Hmm, \"尝试次数计入既有 attempts 限流\" specifically refers to the code's `attempts` field. I'll make sure `confirm` increments `current.attempts` on wrong confirmToken. I'll ALSO apply IP rate limiting for consistency (reuse `redeemRateLimited`). Actually, let me keep it minimal — reuse the same IP limiter for confirm too, since it's the same class of \"guessing a secret\" endpoint. That's good security. But it adds a tiny bit of code. Fine.\n\nHmm, wait — but the store `attempts` is shared between `redeem` and `confirm` on the SAME code record. If both are used, they share the counter. That's \"既有 attempts 限流\" — yes, the existing attempts field. Good.\n\nNow, the `PAIR_TWO_STEP` switch and `redeem` gating:\n- When `PAIR_TWO_STEP=true` (default): should `/api/v1/pair/redeem` still work? \n\nLet me make a final call. Given the analysis, I'll gate `redeem` at the HTTP level: when `PAIR_TWO_STEP=true`, `/api/v1/pair/redeem` returns `410 {\"error\":\"two_step_required\"}` (pointing to begin/confirm). When false, it works normally. This makes \"只扫码不能完成\" TRUE by default and \"false → 走旧单段\" TRUE. And I'll update the http probe §30 to run with `PAIR_TWO_STEP=false`.\n\nBut then — the default desktop `/pair` page + old QR flow is broken by default (QR code can't be redeemed, and there's no confirmToken UI). I'll document this clearly as a known boundary: \"本批只交付 begin/confirm 接口（接口先行）；电脑端配对页与手机端两段式交互未接（另说），默认 true 下旧 /pair 单段页因 redeem 被收紧而不再能完成配对，需 PAIR_TWO_STEP=false 回滚或后续接 UI\". Hmm, that's a concerning boundary — default config makes the existing pairing page broken. \n\nActually — you know what, let me reconsider ONE more time. I keep going back and forth. Let me think about what a reasonable engineer would ship given \"接口先就位，手机端接不接是它的事\" + \"为了安全默认开\" + \"保留旧单段回滚用\".\n\nI think the KEY insight I've been missing: maybe the switch should NOT disable `redeem`. Instead, the switch should control whether `begin`/`confirm` are the ACTIVE path, but `redeem` is kept purely as a rollback artifact. The phrase \"保留旧的单段 `POST /pairing/redeem`（回滚用）\" — \"回滚用\" = \"for rollback use\". This suggests `redeem` is kept so that when you flip the switch off, you fall back to it. It does NOT necessarily mean redeem is disabled when the switch is ON. But \"false → 走旧单段\" implies true → 走两段式.\n\nHmm, but if redeem is available in true mode, then the security semantic is violated as I discussed.\n\nOK you know what — let me look at how OTHER rollback switches in this codebase behave, to follow the established pattern. E.g., `CHANCELLOR_ENABLED=false` → \"回到 8 个工具\" (from AGENTS.md). Let me look at `chatContextLookupEnabled` (the aroundIndex switch from batch 20) since §2 reuses it, and `recallSessionsEnabled`. Let me see how those switches gate endpoints. This will give me the house style.\n\nLet me read chat-context.ts (the switch) and how index.ts uses `chatContextLookupEnabled` at the context endpoint (around line 1247-1310). And flags.ts to understand env + flag overrides.\n\nActually — the switch pattern matters. Let me read the context endpoint fully and chat-context.ts.",
