        "text": "There's no \"vision\" use in the codebase. The `AUX_USES` are `[\"title\", \"compact\", \"review\", \"extract\"]`. \n\nThe task §3 says \"title 与 vision 的显式不适用\". Hmm. Let me re-read the task carefully once more:\n\n\"## 三、auxiliary 剩余：title 与 vision 的**显式不适用**\n3.1 已核实：没有自动标题功能、没有 vision 场景 —— **没有调用点**。\n3.2 但\"没有调用点\"不该只写在变更记录里。要做：\n   - `auxiliary.ts` 里给 `title` / `vision` 两个用途加**显式注释**说明\"当前无调用点，保留接口是因为 XXX（未来做会话自动命名 / 图片理解时直接用）\"；\n   - `auxiliaryModel(\"title\")` / `(\"vision\")` **调用时打一条 warn**（只一次），提示\"该用途当前无调用方，配置不会生效\"——避免有人配了以为生效。\n3.3 单测：配了 title/vision → 返回配置值但打 warn（warn 可注入以便断言）。\"\n\nHmm. So the task explicitly references `auxiliaryModel(\"vision\")`. But there's no `vision` use. \n\nPossibilities:\n1. The task author made an error and meant `title` and `compact` (the actual two \"no call site\" uses). \n2. The task wants me to ADD a `vision` use (pure increment) representing \"图片理解\" (image understanding), with no call site, annotated as such.\n3. \"vision\" is a typo/loose term for `compact`.\n\nLet me think about which makes the most sense. The batch 23b/26b comment says the \"没接\" (not wired) uses are `title` and `compact`. And `compact` is \"内核 Conversation.compact() 只收 instructions + Context...无法指定单独的压缩模型\". So `compact` has NO call site effectively (the config doesn't take effect — there's a warn in session.ts:117 about it).\n\nHmm wait — actually session.ts:117 has `console.warn(\"[aux] 当前内核不支持指定压缩模型，AUX_MODEL_COMPACT 未生效\")`. So there IS already a warn for compact (in `startChatCompaction`). So compact is already handled with an explicit \"not effective\" warn (batch 26b). So §3 \"auxiliary 剩余\" (remaining) would be about `title` — which has NO warn and NO call site.\n\nSo the \"remaining\" work for auxiliary is really about `title` (no call site, no warn). But the task says \"title 与 vision\". \n\nHmm. Let me reconsider — maybe the task author thinks of the 4 uses as: title (auto-naming), vision (image understanding), review (judge), extract (preference). I.e., they might have MISREAD `compact` as `vision`. OR the task is from a context where `compact` was renamed.\n\nActually — you know what, I bet the task author is using \"vision\" to loosely refer to a \"图片理解\" use that they THINK exists or should exist. Given 3.2 explicitly says \"未来做会话自动命名 / 图片理解时直接用\" (future auto-naming / image understanding) and 3.3 says \"配了 title/vision → 返回配置值但打 warn\", the task clearly wants TWO uses: `title` and `vision`, both with no call site, both warn on call.\n\nGiven there's no `vision` in `AuxUse`, I have two reasonable implementations:\n(A) Add `vision` to `AuxUse` + `AUX_USES` (pure increment: a new use with no call site), annotate both `title` and `vision` as \"no call site\", and warn on both.\n(B) Interpret \"vision\" as actually `compact` and annotate `title` + `compact`.\n\nHmm. Which is correct? Let me think about the risk:\n- (A) adds a new use `vision` — this changes `AUX_USES` (and the existing test asserts `[...AUX_USES] === [\"title\",\"compact\",\"review\",\"extract\"]`). I'd need to update that test. Adding a use is a \"contract\" change (new `AUX_MODEL_VISION` env). Per AGENTS.md, \"新能力给回滚开关\" and \"接口契约\" changes need a 设计方案. But adding a use that's NEVER called is harmless. Still, it changes the tool-facing enum.\n- (B) reinterprets \"vision\" as `compact` — doesn't add anything, but MISinterprets the task (the task explicitly says vision/图片理解, not compact/压缩).\n\nHmm. Let me reconsider by re-reading the auxiliary.ts \"接线状态\" comment: it says `title` (no auto-title) and `compact` (kernel can't) are \"没接\". And `review`/`extract` are \"已接\". So the two uses WITHOUT a real call site are `title` and `compact`. \n\nWait — actually, re-reading: `compact` IS \"called\" — `startChatCompaction` in session.ts calls... let me check. session.ts:117 warns \"当前内核不支持指定压缩模型，AUX_MODEL_COMPACT 未生效\". So `startChatCompaction` does NOT call `auxiliaryModel(\"compact\")` — it just warns that the config doesn't work. So `auxiliaryModel(\"compact\")` is NEVER called anywhere (only tested in auxiliary.test.ts). Let me verify: grep showed `auxiliaryModel` calls at: memory-consolidate.ts:113 (`review`), memory-extract.ts:60 (`extract`), and auxiliary.test.ts (tests for title/compact/extract/review). So `auxiliaryModel(\"title\")` and `auxiliaryModel(\"compact\")` are ONLY called in tests — NO production call site. That's the \"没有调用点\" fact.\n\nSo the two uses with NO production call site are `title` and `compact`. \n\nHmm. So the task's \"vision\" is likely a mistake for... no. Actually — wait. Let me reconsider: maybe the task author intends for me to RENAME `compact` to `vision`? No, that'd be a breaking change.\n\nOK let me think about this differently. The task is explicit and I should follow it. It says:\n- Annotate `title` / `vision` as \"no call site\".\n- `auxiliaryModel(\"title\")` / `(\"vision\")` → warn once.\n- Test: configured title/vision → returns config value but warns.\n\nFor `auxiliaryModel(\"vision\")` to be valid, `vision` must be an `AuxUse`. So the task REQUIRES a `vision` use to exist (or be added). Since it doesn't exist, I should ADD it. But wait — would adding `vision` break the existing \"4 uses\" assumption? Let me check the auxiliary.test.ts line 54: `assert.deepEqual([...AUX_USES], [\"title\", \"compact\", \"review\", \"extract\"])`. If I add `vision`, I'd update this to include it. That's fine (I'm editing the test anyway for §3.3).\n\nHmm, but adding a NEW use that has NO functionality and NO call site is a bit odd. But the task explicitly frames it as \"保留接口是因为 XXX（未来做...图片理解时直接用）\" — i.e., KEEP the interface for FUTURE image understanding. So \"保留接口\" implies the interface ALREADY exists. But `vision` doesn't exist. Contradiction.\n\nWait — unless `vision` is meant to be a use that was PLANNED but I should add. Hmm.\n\nLet me reconsider — maybe I'm wrong and there's a different reading. Let me re-read 3.1: \"已核实：没有自动标题功能、没有 vision 场景 —— 没有调用点\". \"没有 vision 场景\" = \"there is no vision scenario\". This says there's no vision SCENARIO (no place where vision is used). It doesn't say there's no vision INTERFACE. Hmm. So maybe the task author believes there's a `vision` use configured but no scenario using it.\n\nI think the most likely scenario: the task author is working from a slightly different mental model / an earlier plan where the uses included `vision`. But the actual code has `compact`. \n\nGiven the ambiguity, let me make a decision that:\n1. Honors the task's explicit intent: TWO uses (`title` and `vision`) annotated as \"no call site\" + warn on call + test.\n2. Doesn't break existing behavior.\n\nI'll ADD `vision` to `AuxUse` and `AUX_USES`, annotated as \"no call site, kept for future image understanding\". AND I'll ALSO handle `compact` and `title` since they're the ACTUAL no-call-site uses. Hmm, but the task says specifically title + vision.\n\nHmm, wait. Actually — let me reconsider. Maybe the cleanest and most defensible: treat \"vision\" as the task's name for the SECOND no-call-site use, and realize that in the CURRENT code that's `compact`. But the task says \"图片理解\" (image understanding) for vision, which maps to a use that doesn't exist. \n\nUgh. Let me look at whether there's any prior design doc mentioning a `vision` auxiliary use. Let me grep the docs for \"vision\" / \"图片理解\" / \"auxiliary 用途\".\n\nActually, let me reconsider the possibility that the task literally wants me to ADD a `vision` use. Re-reading 3.2: \"给 title / vision 两个用途加显式注释说明'当前无调用点，保留接口是因为 XXX（未来做会话自动命名 / 图片理解时直接用）'\". \"保留接口\" — keep the interface. For `vision`, \"保留接口\" would mean the `vision` use exists in the enum. If it doesn't, I need to add it so there's an interface to keep. Adding `AUX_MODEL_VISION` support is a pure increment (new optional env var, new enum member, no behavior change for existing uses). \n\nHmm, but is adding a use \"与本需求无关\"? No — the task explicitly asks for `vision`. \n\nOK — let me make a decision. I'll go with **(A)**: ADD `vision` as a new `AuxUse` (pure increment), with `title` and `vision` both:\n- Annotated in auxiliary.ts as \"当前无调用点，保留接口是因为未来做会话自动命名 / 图片理解时直接用\".\n- `auxiliaryModel(\"title\")` and `auxiliaryModel(\"vision\")` → warn once (\"该用途当前无调用方，配置不会生效\").\n- Tests: configured title/vision → returns the configured value AND warns (warn injectable).\n\nBut wait — what about `compact`? It ALSO has no production call site (only tested). Should I warn on `compact` too? The task says \"title 与 vision\". Hmm. But `compact` already has a warn in session.ts:117 (startChatCompaction), but that's not in `auxiliaryModel`. Actually `auxiliaryModel(\"compact\")` is never called in production, so no warn would ever fire for it in production. But the task focuses on title/vision. \n\nHmm — actually, wait. Let me reconsider. The `compact` use is arguably \"无调用点\" too. But batch 26b explicitly decided to KEEP `compact` resolvable (returns pinned model) with the \"not effective\" fact logged by `startChatCompaction` — i.e., it's an intentional, documented state, NOT a silent gap. The auxiliary.test.ts line 134-138 comment says: \"compact 用途能解析：配了返回 pin 的模型...绝不静默失效（未生效的事实由 startChatCompaction 记日志）\". So `compact` is INTENTIONALLY handled. \n\nSo the \"剩余\" (remaining) gap is really `title` — which has NO annotation, NO warn, NO call site. And the task adds `vision` as a second one. \n\nOK. Decision: I'll implement (A). Add `vision` to the enum, annotate `title` + `vision` as no-call-site, warn on both. I'll also mention `compact` in the annotation for completeness (it's intentionally handled elsewhere) but the WARN will be for the \"no call site\" uses.\n\nHmm — wait, but actually, let me reconsider whether warning should apply to `compact` too. The task says \"auxiliaryModel(\"title\") / (\"vision\") 调用时打一条 warn（只一次）\". So warn for title and vision. If I add `vision`, I should ALSO consider: does `compact` need a warn? The task doesn't mention it. But `auxiliaryModel(\"compact\")` has no production call site either. Hmm. To be safe and consistent, let me define a set `NO_CALL_SITE_USES = [\"title\", \"vision\"]` (and maybe `compact`?). Actually — let me keep it focused on exactly what the task says: `title` and `vision`. I'll define which uses are \"no call site\" as `title` + `vision` (the two the task names). For `compact`, it's a separate intentional case (documented in batch 26b), so I won't warn on it (to avoid contradicting the existing \"compact 能解析，绝不静默失效\" test semantics — actually a warn doesn't break that test, but let me keep scope tight).\n\nHmm — but wait, there's a subtlety: the existing test `\"pin 只在别的供应商里有 → 用那个供应商\"` uses `auxiliaryModel(\"title\", ...)` and asserts the returned model. If I add a warn on title, that test will still pass (it doesn't check warn absence). But it'll print a warn to console during tests. That's fine. But to assert the warn, I need an INJECTABLE warn (task: \"warn 可注入以便断言\"). So I'll add `warn?: (message: string) => void` to `AuxiliaryDeps`. Default `console.warn`. Then tests inject a spy.\n\n\"只一次\" (only once) — the warn should fire only once per use (not every call). Hmm — \"调用时打一条 warn（只一次）\". Does \"只一次\" mean \"one warn per call\" or \"one warn total (once, ever)\"? Let me interpret as \"只一次\" = dedupe — warn once per process per use, so repeated calls don't spam. Actually — re-reading: \"调用时打一条 warn（只一次）\" — \"when called, emit one warn (only once)\". I think \"只一次\" means the warn is emitted once (not repeated on every call). Let me implement a module-level `Set<AuxUse>` of warned uses, so each no-call-site use warns once per process. But that makes tests tricky (state leaks between tests). Hmm. \n\nAlternatively, \"只一次\" could mean \"emit A single warn line per call\" (i.e., just one line, not multiple). That's simpler and stateless. Let me re-read: \"调用时打一条 warn（只一次），提示...\". \"打一条 warn（只一次）\" — \"emit one warn (just once)\". I think it mean