ate, the test needs to reset it. Let me design:\n\n```ts\nexport interface AuxiliaryDeps {\n  env?: NodeJS.ProcessEnv;\n  current?: ModelRef | null;\n  models?: AuxModelLookup;\n  /** 注入 warn 以便单测断言；缺省 console.warn */\n  warn?: (message: string) => void;\n  /** 注入\"已告警用途\"集合以便单测隔离；缺省进程内单例（只告警一次） */\n  warned?: Set<string>;\n}\n\nconst warnedNoCallSite = new Set<string>();  // 进程内：\"只一次\"\n\nexport function auxiliaryModel(use, deps = {}): ModelRef | null {\n  ...\n  // 显式\"无调用点\"用途：调用即 warn 一次，提示配置不会生效\n  const noCallSite = NO_CALL_SITE_USES.has(use);\n  if (noCallSite) {\n    const warned = deps.warned ?? warnedNoCallSite;\n    if (!warned.has(use)) {\n      warned.add(use);\n      (deps.warn ?? console.warn)(\n        `[aux] ${use} 用途当前无调用方，AUX_MODEL_${use.toUpperCase()} 配置不会生效`,\n      );\n    }\n  }\n  ... // 继续正常解析（返回配置值）\n```\n\nWait — but WHERE should this warn go? The task says \"调用时打一条 warn\" — emit when called. It should warn regardless of whether a model is pinned? \"配了以为生效\" (configured and thought it took effect). Hmm. The warn is about \"配置不会生效\" (config won't take effect). Should it warn only when a model IS pinned? Or always? Let me re-read: \"auxiliaryModel(\"title\") / (\"vision\") 调用时打一条 warn（只一次），提示\"该用途当前无调用方，配置不会生效\"——避免有人配了以为生效。\" So it warns on CALL, to tell people \"even if you configured it, it won't take effect\". I think warn on every call (deduped) regardless of pin. Actually — hmm, but if someone calls `auxiliaryModel(\"title\")` with NO pin, warning \"config won't take effect\" is slightly odd (nothing configured). But the message is about the USE having no call site, so it's fine to warn on any call. Let me warn on any call to title/vision (deduped once). \n\nActually — wait, but there's a subtlety: `auxiliaryModel` returns `null` early if `!current` (no current model). Should the warn fire even then? Let me place the warn at the TOP of the function (right after determining env), so it fires on every call to a no-call-site use. That's \"调用时\". Hmm, but then the existing test `\"没有当前模型 → null\"` uses `auxiliaryModel(\"extract\", {current: null})` — not a no-call-site use, so no warn. Fine.\n\nBut — hmm, placing the warn at the top means it fires even when `current` is null. That's fine (it's about the use, not the model).\n\nAlso — the task §3.3: \"配了 title/vision → 返回配置值但打 warn\". So the test: configure `AUX_MODEL_TITLE=small-model`, call `auxiliaryModel(\"title\", {current: CURRENT, models: fakeModels(), warn: spy, warned: freshSet})`, assert result is the pinned model AND spy called once. Good.\n\nBut WAIT — there's a conflict: the EXISTING test `\"pin 只在别的供应商里有 → 用那个供应商\"` calls `auxiliaryModel(\"title\", {current, env: {AUX_MODEL_TITLE: \"tiny-model\"}, models})` and asserts `{provider:\"other\", modelId:\"tiny-model\"}`. With my warn, this still works (warn is deduped via module-level set, prints to console once). Fine — no assertion on warn there. But it WILL consume the \"once\" for `title` in the module-level set. Then my new test, if it uses the module-level set, would NOT get a warn (already warned). That's why I need the injectable `warned` set in tests. Good — my new test passes `warned: new Set()` to get a fresh dedupe scope. \n\nHmm, but actually — there's still a subtlety: the module-level `warnedNoCallSite` set persists across ALL tests in the file. If test A (existing) calls `auxiliaryModel(\"title\")` and triggers a console.warn, and test B (new) injects `warned: new Set()`, test B gets its own scope → warn fires → assert passes. Good. But the console.warn from test A would print during `pnpm test` — that's noisy but harmless. Actually — hmm, let me reconsider: should I avoid console.warn noise in existing tests? The existing tests call `auxiliaryModel(\"title\")` and `auxiliaryModel(\"compact\")`. With warn on `title` (no-call-site), the existing test `\"pin 只在别的供应商里有\"` would trigger a console.warn. That's a bit noisy but acceptable. Alternatively, I could scope the dedupe/warn such that it only warns when there's a PIN... no, keep it simple.\n\nActually — hold on. Let me reconsider whether to warn on `title` at all given the existing test confirms `title` resolves a pinned model (returns \"other\"/\"tiny-model\"). The task says warn on title. So `title` resolves the config value BUT warns that it has no call site / config won't take effect. That's consistent with §3.3 \"返回配置值但打 warn\". Good.\n\nNow — about adding `vision` to `AuxUse`. Let me reconsider ONE more time whether that's right. The alternative (B): interpret \"vision\" as `compact` — but `compact` is about COMPACTION (compression), not \"图片理解\" (image understanding). The task's parenthetical \"（未来做会话自动命名 / 图片理解时直接用）\" clearly maps: 会话自动命名 → title, 图片理解 → vision. So `vision` = image understanding, a distinct use. Since it doesn't exist, I must add it. \n\nHmm, but wait — adding a NEW use `vision` might be considered scope creep / a contract change requiring a 设计方案. But the task EXPLICITLY asks for `vision` with `auxiliaryModel(\"vision\")` being callable. So adding it is necessary to satisfy the task. I'll add it as a pure increment (new enum member, new optional env `AUX_MODEL_VISION`, NO call site, annotated). I'll note in the change record that `vision` is a new reserved use with no call site.\n\nActually — hmm, wait. Let me reconsider: is it possible the task author just confused `compact` with `vision` and the SAFEST implementation is to treat the two \"no call site\" uses as `title` and `compact` (the actual ones)? Let me weigh:\n- If I ADD `vision` and the author meant `compact`, I've added an extra use that wasn't wanted (minor scope creep) but ALSO didn't handle `compact` annotation/warn. Hmm.\n- If I treat \"vision\"=`compact` and the author meant a new `vision`, I've failed to add `vision`.\n\nGiven the task is SO explicit (\"auxiliaryModel(\"vision\")\", \"配了 title/vision\", \"图片理解\"), I'll ADD `vision`. But I'll ALSO handle `compact` gracefully — actually, let me r