ion 场景 —— 没有调用点\". \"没有 vision 场景\" = \"there is no vision scenario\". This says there's no vision SCENARIO (no place where vision is used). It doesn't say there's no vision INTERFACE. Hmm. So maybe the task author believes there's a `vision` use configured but no scenario using it.\n\nI think the most likely scenario: the task author is working from a slightly different mental model / an earlier plan where the uses included `vision`. But the actual code has `compact`. \n\nGiven the ambiguity, let me make a decision that:\n1. Honors the task's explicit intent: TWO uses (`title` and `vision`) annotated as \"no call site\" + warn on call + test.\n2. Doesn't break existing behavior.\n\nI'll ADD `vision` to `AuxUse` and `AUX_USES`, annotated as \"no call site, kept for future image understanding\". AND I'll ALSO handle `compact` and `title` since they're the ACTUAL no-call-site uses. Hmm, but the task says specifically title + vision.\n\nHmm, wait. Actually — let me reconsider. Maybe the cleanest and most defensible: treat \"vision\" as the task's name for the SECOND no-call-site use, and realize that in the CURRENT code that's `compact`. But the task says \"图片理解\" (image understanding) for vision, which maps to a use that doesn't exist. \n\nUgh. Let me look at whether there's any prior design doc mentioning a `vision` auxiliary use. Let me grep the docs for \"vision\" / \"图片理解\" / \"auxiliary 用途\".\n\nActually, let me reconsider the possibility that the task literally wants me to ADD a `vision` use. Re-reading 3.2: \"给 title / vision 两个用途加显式注释说明'当前无调用点，保留接口是因为 XXX（未来做会话自动命名 / 图片理解时直接用）'\". \"保留接口\" — keep the interface. For `vision`, \"保留接口\" would mean the `vision` use exists in the enum. If it doesn't, I need to add it so there's an interface to keep. Adding `AUX_MODEL_VISION` support is a pure increment (new optional env var, new enum member, no behavior change for existing uses). \n\nHmm, but is adding a use \"与本需求无关\"? No — the task explicitly asks for `vision`. \n\nOK — let me make a decision. I'll go with **(A)**: ADD `vision` as a new `AuxUse` (pure increment), with `title` and `vision` both:\n- Annotated in auxiliary.ts as \"当前无调用点，保留接口是因为未来做会话自动命名 / 图片理解时直接用\".\n- `auxiliaryModel(\"title\")` and `auxiliaryModel(\"vision\")` → warn once (\"该用途当前无调用方，配置不会生效\").\n- Tests: configured title/vision → returns the configured value AND warns (warn injectable).\n\nBut wait — what about `compact`? It ALSO has no production call site (only tested). Should I warn on `compact` too? The task says \"title 与 vision\". Hmm. But `compact` already has a warn in session.ts:117 (startChatCompaction), but that's not in `auxiliaryModel`. Actually `auxiliaryModel(\"compact\")` is never called in production, so no warn would ever fire for it in production. But the task focuses on title/vision. \n\nHmm — actually, wait. Let me reconsider. The `compact` use is arguably \"无调用点\" too. But batch 26b explicitly decided to KEEP `compact` resolvable (returns pinned model) with the \"not effective\" fact logged by `startChatCompaction` — i.e., it's an intentional, documented state, NOT a silent gap. The auxiliary.test.ts line 134-138 comment says: \"compact 用途能解析：配了返回 pin 的模型...绝不静默失效（未生效的事实由 startChatCompaction 记日志）\". So `compact` is INTENTIONALLY handled. \n\nSo the \"剩余\" (remaining) gap is really `title` — which has NO annotation, NO warn, NO call site. And the task adds `vision` as a second one. \n\nOK. Decision: I'll implement (A). Add `vision` to the enum, annotate `title` + `vision` as no-call-site, warn on both. I'll also mention `compact` in the annotation for completeness (it's intentionally handled elsewhere) but the WARN will be for the \"no call site\" uses.\n\nHmm — wait, but actually, let me reconsider whether warning should apply to `compact` too. The task says \"auxiliaryModel(\"title\") / (\"vision\") 调用时打一条 warn（只一次）\". So warn for title and vision. If I add `vision`, I should ALSO consider: does `compact` need a warn? The task doesn't mention it. But `auxiliaryModel(\"compact\")` has no production call site either. Hmm. To be safe and consistent, let me define a set `NO_CALL_SITE_USES = [\"title\", \"vision\"]` (and maybe `compact`?). Actually — let me keep it focused on exactly what the task says: `title` and `vision`. I'll define which uses are \"no call site\" as `title` + `vision` (the two the task names). For `compact`, it's a separate intentional case (documented in batch 26b), so I won't warn on it (to avoid contradicting the existing \"compact 能解析，绝不静默失效\" test semantics — actually a warn doesn't break that test, but let me keep scope tight).\n\nHmm — but wait, there's a subtlety: the existing test `\"pin 只在别的供应商里有 → 用那个供应商\"` uses `auxiliaryModel(\"title\", ...)` and asserts the returned model. If I add a warn on title, that test will still pass (it doesn't check warn absence). But it'll print a warn to console during tests. That's fine. But to assert the warn, I need an INJECTABLE warn (task: \"warn 可注入以便断言\"). So I'll add `warn?: (message: string) => void` to `AuxiliaryDeps`. Default `console.warn`. Then tests inject a spy.\n\n\"只一次\" (only once) — the warn should fire only once per use (not every call). Hmm — \"调用时打一条 warn（只一次）\". Does \"只一次\" mean \"one warn per call\" or \"one warn total (once, ever)\"? Let me interpret as \"只一次\" = dedupe — warn once per process per use, so repeated calls don't spam. Actually — re-reading: \"调用时打一条 warn（只一次）\" — \"when called, emit one warn (only once)\". I think \"只一次\" means the warn is emitted once (not repeated on every call). Let me implement a module-level `Set<AuxUse>` of warned uses, so each no-call-site use warns once per process. But that makes tests tricky (state leaks between tests). Hmm. \n\nAlternatively, \"只一次\" could mean \"emit A single warn line per call\" (i.e., just one line, not multiple). That's simpler and stateless. Let me re-read: \"调用时打一条 warn（只一次），提示...\". \"打一条 warn（只一次）\" — \"emit one warn (just once)\". I think it means: when `auxiliaryModel` is called with title/vision, emit a single warn line. \"只一次\" emphasizes it's one line, not repeated/spammy. \n\nHmm, but a module-level \"warn once per use\" is also a common pattern. But it introduces global state that complicates testing (and could be reset). Let me go with the simpler interpretation: emit one warn per call (stateless), but make it injectable for tests. Actually — \"只一次\" strongly suggests deduplication. Let me think: if someone configures `AUX_MODEL_TITLE` and `auxiliaryModel(\"title\")` is called, you want to warn \"this has no call site, config won't take effect\". If it's called 100 times, you don't want 100 warns. So \"只一次\" = warn once (dedupe). \n\nLet me implement dedupe with a module-level Set, but make it resettable for tests via the deps (e.g., `warn` injection + a way to reset). Hmm. Actually — to keep it clean and testable, let me implement dedupe with a module-level `Set` AND allow tests to inject both `warn` and use a fresh \"warned\" set. Actually, simplest: add a `warnedUses?: Set<AuxUse>` to deps (defaults to a module-level singleton). Then tests pass a fresh `new Set()`. That way:\n- Production: module-level set, warns once per use per process.\n- Tests: inject a fresh set + a spy warn, assert exactly one warn.\n\nHmm, that's a bit of machinery. Let me reconsider — maybe simpler: just emit one warn per call (no dedupe), and interpret \"只一次\" as \"one line\". Let me re-read the Chinese: \"调用时打一条 warn（只一次）\". \"打一条 warn\" = emit one warn line. \"（只一次）\" = (only once). I now think \"只一次\" means dedupe (warn only once, not on every call). \n\nHmm — but actually, you know what, given the ambiguity, let me implement dedupe in a clean, testable way. I'll use a module-level `Set<string>` and expose it via deps for test isolation. Actually — let me reconsider: the \"warn\" being injectable is explicitly required (\"warn 可注入以便断言\"). So the test wants to assert the warn was called. If I dedupe with module-level state, the test needs to reset it. Let me design:\n\n```ts\nexport interface AuxiliaryDeps {\n  env?: NodeJS.ProcessEnv;\n  current?: ModelRef | null;\n  models?: AuxModelLookup;\n  /** 注入 warn 以便单测断言；缺省 console.warn */\n  warn?: (message: string) => void;\n  /** 注入\"已告警用途\"集合以便单测隔离；缺省进程内单例（只告警一次） */\n  warned?: Set<string>;\n}\n\nconst warnedNoCallSite = new Set<string>();  // 进程内：\"只一次\"\n\nexport function auxiliaryModel(use, deps = {}): ModelRef | null {\n  ...\n  // 显式\"无调用点\"用途：调用即 warn 一次，提示配置不会生效\n  const noCallSite = NO_CALL_SITE_USES.has(use);\n  if (noCallSite) {\n    const warned = deps.warned ?? warnedNoCallSite;\n    if (!warned.has(use)) {\n      warned.add(use);\n      (deps.warn ?? console.warn)(\n        `[aux] ${use} 用途当前无调用方，AUX_MODEL_${use.toUpperCase()} 配置不会生效`,\n      );\n    }\n  }\n  ... // 继续正常解析（返回配置值）\n```\n\nWait — but WHERE should this warn go? The task says \"调用时打一条 warn\" — emit when called. It should warn regardless of whether a model is pinned? \"配了以为生效\" (configured and thought it took effect). Hmm. The warn is about \"配置不会生效\" (config won't take effect). Should it warn only when a model IS pinned? Or always? Let me re-read: \"auxiliaryModel(\"title\") / (\"vision\") 调用时打一条 warn（只一次），提示\"该用途当前无调用方，配置不会生效\"——避免有人配了以为生效。\" So it warns on CALL, to tell people \"even if you configured it, it won't take effect\". I think warn on every call (deduped) regardless of pin. Actually — hmm, but if someone calls `auxiliaryModel(\"title\")` with NO pin, warning \"config won't take effect\" is slightly odd (nothing configured). But the message is about the USE having no call site, so it's fine to warn on any call. Let me warn on any call to title/vision (deduped once). \n\nActually — wait, but there's a subtlety: `auxiliaryModel` returns `null` early if `!current` (no current model). Should the warn fire even then? Let me place the warn at the TOP of the function (right after determining env), so it fires on every call to a no-call-site use. That