warn such that it only warns when there's a PIN... no, keep it simple.\n\nActually — hold on. Let me reconsider whether to warn on `title` at all given the existing test confirms `title` resolves a pinned model (returns \"other\"/\"tiny-model\"). The task says warn on title. So `title` resolves the config value BUT warns that it has no call site / config won't take effect. That's consistent with §3.3 \"返回配置值但打 warn\". Good.\n\nNow — about adding `vision` to `AuxUse`. Let me reconsider ONE more time whether that's right. The alternative (B): interpret \"vision\" as `compact` — but `compact` is about COMPACTION (compression), not \"图片理解\" (image understanding). The task's parenthetical \"（未来做会话自动命名 / 图片理解时直接用）\" clearly maps: 会话自动命名 → title, 图片理解 → vision. So `vision` = image understanding, a distinct use. Since it doesn't exist, I must add it. \n\nHmm, but wait — adding a NEW use `vision` might be considered scope creep / a contract change requiring a 设计方案. But the task EXPLICITLY asks for `vision` with `auxiliaryModel(\"vision\")` being callable. So adding it is necessary to satisfy the task. I'll add it as a pure increment (new enum member, new optional env `AUX_MODEL_VISION`, NO call site, annotated). I'll note in the change record that `vision` is a new reserved use with no call site.\n\nActually — hmm, wait. Let me reconsider: is it possible the task author just confused `compact` with `vision` and the SAFEST implementation is to treat the two \"no call site\" uses as `title` and `compact` (the actual ones)? Let me weigh:\n- If I ADD `vision` and the author meant `compact`, I've added an extra use that wasn't wanted (minor scope creep) but ALSO didn't handle `compact` annotation/warn. Hmm.\n- If I treat \"vision\"=`compact` and the author meant a new `vision`, I've failed to add `vision`.\n\nGiven the task is SO explicit (\"auxiliaryModel(\"vision\")\", \"配了 title/vision\", \"图片理解\"), I'll ADD `vision`. But I'll ALSO handle `compact` gracefully — actually, let me reconsider: should `compact` also warn? The batch 26b already handles compact with a warn in session.ts (startChatCompaction), and the auxiliary.test.ts comment says compact \"绝不静默失效（未生效的事实由 startChatCompaction 记日志）\". So compact is INTENTIONALLY documented. If I add a warn on `auxiliaryModel(\"compact\")`, it might contradict that intent? No — it'd be consistent (both warn). But `auxiliaryModel(\"compact\")` is never called in production, so the warn would never fire there. Only in tests. Hmm.\n\nLet me keep §3 SCOPE TIGHT to exactly what's asked: `title` and `vision`. I'll:\n- Add `vision` to `AuxUse` + `AUX_USES`.\n- Define `NO_CALL_SITE_USES = new Set<AuxUse>([\"title\", \"vision\"])`.\n- Annotate in auxiliary.ts the two uses with explicit \"当前无调用点，保留接口是因为未来做会话自动命名 / 图片理解时直接用\".\n- Warn (deduped once, injectable) on calls to those uses.\n- Tests for both.\n\nAnd update the `AUX_USES` assertion in the existing test to include `vision`.\n\nHmm — wait, actually, hold on. Let me reconsider adding `vision` once more. The existing `AUX_USES` is used in docs/探针. Adding `vision` changes the \"4 uses\" to \"5 uses\". Is there any code that assumes exactly 4? Let me check where `AUX_USES` is used. Earlier grep showed it's imported in auxiliary.test.ts and maybe elsewhere. Let me verify. Actually the grep for `AUX_USES` showed only auxiliary.ts (definition) and auxiliary.test.ts (line 4 import, line 54 assertion). Let me confirm there's no other consumer (e.g., a provider probe that iterates uses). Let me grep more broadly.\n\nActually, let me just do a comprehensive grep for AUX_USES and auxPinnedModelId and AuxUse consumers.",
