reate these. Actually, let me be efficient and just create a handful.\n\nLet me also double check the `web/app.js` — I need to be careful about `node --check`. The user says \"前端改完 node --check（拷 .mjs）\". Meaning: app.js is an ES module? Let me check. The app.js uses `const el = ...` at top level, `import`? Actually it says \"所有网络请求只从这里出去\". Let me check if app.js is a module (uses `import`/`export`) or a plain script. The instruction \"拷 .mjs\" suggests: copy app.js to a `.mjs` file and run `node --check` on it (because app.js might be a classic script but node --check on .js treats it as CommonJS; copying to .mjs treats as ESM). Actually — `node --check app.js` works on any JS file for SYNTAX checking (it doesn't execute). But if app.js uses `import`/`export` (ESM), `node --check app.js` might complain about top-level import in a CJS context? Actually `node --check` on a .js file with `import` statements: Node would try to parse as CommonJS (since package.json type isn't module) and `import` at top level is a syntax error in CJS. So copying to `.mjs` forces ESM parsing. Hence \"拷 .mjs\". Let me check if app.js has `import`/`export`. Let me grep.\n\nActually — let me check the index.html to see how app.js is loaded (type=\"module\"?)."
