      {
        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "This confirms it: the 总账 #32 explicitly says \"杂活模型（标题/压缩/vision/评审）\" and \"**title/vision 无调用点**\". So \"vision\" IS a recognized auxiliary use in the ledger — but the `auxiliary.ts` implementation only has 4 uses (title/compact/review/extract), NOT vision. So the ledger's \"vision\" concept was never fully implemented as an `AuxUse`.\n\nSo the task §3 \"title 与 vision 的显式不适用\" maps to the ledger's \"title/vision 无调用点\". The task wants me to:\n- Make `title` and `vision` explicitly annotated as \"no call site\" in auxiliary.ts.\n- Warn on `auxiliaryModel(\"title\")` / `(\"vision\")`.\n\nGiven the ledger treats `vision` as one of the auxiliary uses (标题/压缩/vision/评审 = title/compact/vision/review) — wait, that's 4: title, compact, vision, review. But the code has title, compact, review, extract. So the ledger's \"评审\" (review) + \"vision\" + \"compact\" + \"title\" = 4 uses, while the code has \"extract\" (抽取) instead of \"vision\". Hmm. So the ledger's mental model differs: it lists 标题/压缩/vision/评审, code lists 标题/压缩/评审/抽取 (extract).\n\nHmm. So \"vision\" in the ledger is one of the 4 auxiliary categories (from the hermes reference: \"curator/标题/压缩/vision/群聊路由/smart-approval 各自 pin 小模型\"). So \"vision\" = a use for image/vision tasks. The code never added `vision` as an `AuxUse` (it added `extract` instead).\n\nOK — so the task §3 wants `vision` to be an explicit \"no call site\" use. The cleanest realization: ADD `vision` to `AuxUse`/`AUX_USES` (making 5 uses: title, compact, vision, review, extract), annotate `title` + `vision` as no-call-site, warn on both. This aligns with the ledger's concept. \n\nActually — wait. Hmm. Let me reconsider: maybe the task intends `vision` to be a NEW 5th use reserved for future image understanding. Given the ledger lists \"标题/压缩/vision/评审\" as the 4 categories and the code has \"标题/压缩/评审/抽取\", there's a mismatch. But the task explicitly says \"title 与 vision\" (the two no-call-site ones). And 3.2 \"未来做会话自动命名 / 图片理解时直接用\" (future auto-naming / image understanding). So:\n- `title` → 会话自动命名 (auto-naming) — EXISTS in code.\n- `vision` → 图片理解 (image understanding) — does NOT exist in code → ADD it.\n\nSo I'll ADD `vision` as a 5th use. Let me finalize. This also means `AUX_USES` becomes 5 elements. I'll update the test assertion.\n\nHmm — but wait, does adding a 5th use require a 设计方案 per AGENTS.md? \"接口契约（新增 / 改名 / 语义变化）\" → 必须先写方案. Adding a new `AuxUse` enum member + `AUX_MODEL_VISION` env is arguably a contract change. BUT — the task book IS the design document (it's in `docs/设计方案/`). And the task explicitly instructs it. Also, adding a reserved, non-functional use is a \"纯增量\" that doesn't change existing behavior. I'll treat the task book as the design decision and document in the change record. Actually — to be safe, I'll note in the change record that this is a pure-increment reservation (no call site, inert config) explicitly requested by the task book, and that it doesn't alter existing use semantics.\n\nHmm, OK — but actually, let me reconsider ONE more time: is it cleaner to NOT add `vision` and instead interpret `vision` as `compact`? NO — the task explicitly says `auxiliaryModel(\"vision\")` and \"图片理解\". And the ledger confirms `vision` is a distinct concept. Adding it is correct. Let me do it.\n\nActually — hold on, wait. Let me reconsider yet again. Hmm — actually, I realize there might be an even simpler reading that avoids adding a new use: maybe the task wants me to treat `title` and `compact` (the actual no-call-site uses in code) but CALLS the second one \"vision\". But 3.2 says \"图片理解\" (image understanding) for the second — which is NOT compact (compression). And the ledger explicitly separates \"压缩\" (compact) and \"vision\". So `vision` ≠ `compact`. So I must add `vision`.\n\nOK. FINAL: add `vision` as a 5th use. Let me now also reconsider: should `compact` ALSO be in the \"no call site\" warn set? The ledger says \"title/vision 无调用点\" — so compact is NOT listed as \"无调用点\" (because batch 26b handled it with a log). So compact is excluded from the warn set. Good — warn set = {title, vision} only. \n\nNow let me carefully design auxiliary.ts changes:\n\n```ts\nexport type AuxUse = \"title\" | \"compact\" | \"vision\" | \"review\" | \"extract\";\n\n/** 用途清单... */\nexport const AUX_USES: readonly AuxUse[] = [\"title\", \"compact\", \"vision\", \"review\", \"extract\"];\n\n/**\n * 当前无调用点的用途（2026-11-10 批 28 §三）...\n * title：当前没有自动标题功能；保留接口是为了将来做「会话自动命名」时直接用。\n * vision：当前没有 vision 场景（图片理解尚未接入）；保留接口是为了将来做「图片理解」时直接用。\n * 这两项配置了 AUX_MODEL_<USE> 也不会有人来调用 —— auxiliaryModel 被调用时打一条 warn，\n * 避免\"配了以为生效\"。\n */\nconst NO_CALL_SITE_USES: ReadonlySet<AuxUse> = new Set<AuxUse>([\"title\", \"vision\"]);\n\n/** 进程内\"只告警一次\"记账；单测可注入独立 Set 隔离。 */\nconst warnedNoCallSite = new Set<AuxUse>();\n\nexport interface AuxiliaryDeps {\n  env?: NodeJS.ProcessEnv;\n  current?: ModelRef | null;\n  models?: AuxModelLookup;\n  /** 注入 warn 以便单测断言（缺省 console.warn）。 */\n  warn?: (message: string) => void;\n  /** 注入\"已告警用途\"集合以便单测隔离（缺省进程内单例，只告警一次）。 */\n  warned?: Set<AuxUse>;\n}\n```\n\nIn `auxiliaryModel`, after `const env = deps.env ?? process.env;`:\n```ts\nif (NO_CALL_SITE_USES.has(use)) {\n  const warned = deps.warned ?? warnedNoCallSite;\n  if (!warned.has(use)) {\n    warned.add(use);\n    (deps.warn ?? console.warn)(\n      `[aux] ${use} 用途当前无调用方，AUX_MODEL_${use.toUpperCase()} 配置不会生效`,\n    );\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWait — placement: should this be BEFORE the `if (!current) return null;` check? The task says \"调用时打一条 warn\" — emit on call. Let me place it at the very top (after env), so it fires on every call to title/vision (deduped). That's \"调用时\". Good. But — hmm, if `current` is null (no model), should it still warn? Yes — the warn is about the USE having no call site, independent of model availability. Fine.\n\nBut — WAIT. There's a subtle issue: the existing test `\"pin 只在别的供应商里有 → 用那个供应商\"` calls `auxiliaryModel(\"title\", {current: CURRENT, env: {...}, models})`. With my change, this triggers a `console.warn` (since `warned` uses the module-level set and `warn` defaults to console.warn). That will print a warn line during tests. Harmless but noisy. Also, it will consume the \"once\" for `title` in the module-level set. My NEW test injects `warned: new Set<AuxUse>()` so it gets a fresh scope → warn fires → assertion passes. Good.\n\nHmm — but actually, there's a concern: if the existing tests run BEFORE my new test and consume the module-level `warnedNoCallSite` for `title`, and my new test uses `warned: new Set()` — fine, isolated. But what if my new test ALSO wants to verify \"只一次\" (dedupe)? I'll test dedupe within the injected set: call twice with the same injected set + spy, assert spy called once. Good.\n\nAlso — the message \"该用途当前无调用方，配置不会生效\" — let me match the task's wording: \"提示'该用途当前无调用方，配置不会生效'\". I'll use: `[aux] ${use} 用途当前无调用方，AUX_MODEL_${use.toUpperCase()} 配置不会生效`. Good.\n\nNow — §3.3 test: \"配了 title/vision → 返回配置值但打 warn（warn 可注入以便断言）\". So:\n```ts\ntest(\"title / vision 显式无调用点：配了返回配置值，但调用时打一条 warn（只一次）\", () => {\n  for (const use of [\"title\", \"vision\"] as const) {\n    const warns: string[] = [];\n    const warned = new Set<AuxUse>();\n    const deps = {\n      current: CURRENT,\n      env: { [`AUX_MODEL_${use.toUpperCase()}`]: \"small-model\" },\n      models: fakeModels(),\n      warn: (m: string) => warns.push(m),\n      warned,\n    };\n    const result = auxiliaryModel(use, deps);\n    assert.deepEqual(result, { provider: \"bailian\", modelId: \"small-model\" }, `${use} 配了要返回配置值`);\n    assert.equal(warns.length, 1, `${use} 调用要打一条 warn`);\n    assert.match(warns[0]!, /无调用方.*不会生效/);\n    // 再调一次：同一 warned 集合只打一次\n    auxiliaryModel(use, deps);\n    assert.equal(warns.length, 1, `${use} 只告警一次`);\n  }\n});\n```\nWait — `fakeModels()` has `small-model` in `bailian`. `CURRENT = {provider:\"bailian\", modelId:\"big-model\"}`. So pinning `small-model` → `{provider:\"bailian\", modelId:\"small-model\"}`. Good.\n\nNeed to import `AuxUse` type. And update the `AUX_USES` assertion to include `vision`.\n\nAlso — I should add a test that `extract`/`review` (wired uses) do NOT warn. Actually — let me add: \"已接用途不 warn\". Good practice. But the existing tests call `auxiliaryModel(\"extract\", ...)` without a `warn` dep → uses module set + console.warn, but since `extract` is NOT in NO_CALL_SITE_USES, no warn. Fine. I could add an explicit assertion. Let me add a small one.\n\nOK. Now let me also handle the docs env table. Actually — let me reconsider whether adding `vision` REQUIRES updating 接口文档.md §6 env table. The `AUX_LLM` row lists the 4 uses; I should add `vision`. And the `AUX_MODEL_<USE>` row — I should mention `vision` is a reserved no-call-site use. Also add `PAIR_TWO_STEP` to §6. And add the new endpoints to §5 (pairing) and a sessions/search row. Let me do all in the doc-update step.\n\nNow — let me START implementing. I'll begin with §1 pairing.ts. Let me write the changes carefully.\n\nLet me re-read the exact current redeem() to extract the device-issuing helper.\n\nCurrent redeem (lines 188-223):\n```ts\nredeem(code: string, deviceName: string, now = Date.now()): RedeemResult | RedeemError {\n  const current = this.store.code;\n  if (!current) return \"unknown_code\";\n  if (current.usedAt) return \"code_used\";\n  if (current.expiresAt <= now) return \"code_expired\";\n  if (current.attempts >= MAX_CODE_ATTEMPTS) return \"too_many_attempts\";\n\n  if (!hashEquals(current.hash, sha256(code.trim()))) {\n    current.attempts += 1;\n    this.persist();\n    return current.attempts >= MAX_CODE_ATTEMPTS ? \"too_many_attempts\" : \"unknown_code\";\n  }\n\n  const deviceToken = randomBytes(32).toString(\"base64url\");\n  const tokenHash = sha256(deviceToken);\n  const id = randomBytes(8).toString(\"hex\");\n  const device: StoredDevice = {\n    id,\n    name: deviceName.trim().slice(0, 40) || \"手机\",\n    tokenHash,\n    createdAt: now,\n    ...(deviceFingerprintEnabled() ? { fingerprint: deviceFingerprint(id, tokenHash) } : {}),\n  };\n  current.usedAt = now;\n  // 设备上限：踢掉最久没用过的那台（防无限堆积）\n  this.store.devices = [...this.store.devices, device]\n    .filter((item) => !item.revokedAt)\n    .sort((a, b) => (b.lastSeenAt ?? b.createdAt) - (a.lastSeenAt ?? a.createdAt))\n    .slice(0, MAX_DEVICES);\n  this.persist();\n  return {\n    deviceToken,\n    deviceId: device.id,\n    ...(device.fingerprint ? { fingerprint: device.fingerprint } : {}),\n  };\n}\n```\n\nI'll extract lines 201-222 (device issuance + usedAt + persist + return) into `private issueDevice(deviceName, now): RedeemResult`. Then `redeem` becomes:\n```ts\nredeem(code, deviceName, now): RedeemResult | RedeemError {\n  const current = this.store.code;\n  ... validation ...\n  if (!hashEquals(...)) { ... }\n  return this.issueDevice(deviceName, now);\n}\n```\nWait — but `issueDevice` needs to set `current.usedAt = now`. It can access `this.store.code`. Let me have `issueDevice` set `this.store.code!.usedAt = now`. Hmm — but for `confirm`, I also want to set `confirmUsedAt`. Let me have `issueDevice` set `usedAt` (and the caller sets `confirmUsedAt` before calling, OR `issueDevice` takes a flag). Actually — let me make `issueDevice` handle `usedAt` only, and `confirm` sets `confirmUsedAt` separately before/after. Actually, since `usedAt` already indicates the code is consumed, `confirmUsedAt` is somewhat redundant. But the task says \"confirmToken 一次性\" — the confirmToken must be one-time. Since `usedAt` marks the code used, and `confirm` checks `usedAt`, the confirmToken is implicitly one-time (replay → `code_used`). So I might NOT need a separate `confirmUsedAt`. Let me simplify: `confirm` success sets `usedAt` (via issueDevice), and replay is detected by `usedAt`. The `confirmHash` stays but the code is used. That's \"一次性\". \n\nBut — \"confirmToken 一次性\" specifically: after a successful confirm, the SAME confirmToken can't be used again. Since it's bound to the code (confirmHash on the code record) and the code is marked used, a second confirm → `code_used`. ✓. And a NEW `begin()` replaces `store.code` entirely (new code + new confirmHash), so old confirmToken is invalid. ✓. Good — no separate `confirmUsedAt` needed. Simpler.\n\nSo `StoredCode` gains only `confirmHash?: string`. \n\nHmm — but wait: there's a subtlety. `begin()` sets `this.store.code = { hash, expiresAt, attempts: 0, confirmHash }`. `issueCode()` sets `this.store.code = { hash, expiresAt, attempts: 0 }` (no confirmHash). So `hasLiveCode()`, `codeRemainingSeconds()` work for both. Good.\n\nNow `confirm()`:\n```ts\nconfirm(code: string, confirmToken: string, deviceName: string, now = Date.now()): ConfirmResult | ConfirmError {\n  const current = this.store.code;\n  if (!current) return \"unknown_code\";\n  if (!current.confirmHash) return \"unknown_code\";  // 不是两段式码 → 走 redeem\n  if (current.usedAt) return \"code_used\";           // 一次性 / 重放\n  if (current.expiresAt <= now) return \"code_expired\";\n  if (current.attempts >= MAX_CODE_ATTEMPTS) return \"too_many_attempts\";\n\n  if (!hashEquals(current.hash, sha256(code.trim()))) {\n    current.attempts += 1;\n    this.persist();\n    return current.attempts >= MAX_CODE_ATTEMPTS ? \"too_many_attempts\" : \"unknown_code\";\n  }\n\n  const supplied = confirmToken.trim();\n  if (!supplied || !hashEquals(current.confirmHash, sha256(supplied))) {\n    current.attempts += 1;\n    this.persist();\n    if (current.attempts >= MAX_CODE_ATTEMPTS) return \"too_many_attempts\";\n    return supplied ? \"bad_confirm\" : \"confirm_required\";\n  }\n  return this.issueDevice(deviceName, now);\n}\n```\n\nWait — \"只有 code 不能完成\" — when `confirmToken` is empty string → `confirm_required`. That's the \"只有 code\" case (missing confirmToken). Good. And wrong confirmToken → `bad_confirm`. Good.\n\nHmm — but `hashEquals(current.confirmHash, sha256(supplied))` — `current.confirmHash` is a sha256 hex (64 chars), `sha256(supplied)` is 64 chars. `hashEquals` checks equal length + timingSafeEqual. Good.\n\n`ConfirmError` union: `unknown_code | confirm_required | bad_confirm | code_used | code_expired | too_many_attempts`. Let me define it. Actually — let me reconsider: should I reuse `RedeemError`? No, keep separate `ConfirmError`. And `ConfirmResult = RedeemResult`.\n\nNow `begin()`:\n```ts\nbegin(now = Date.now()): { code: string; expiresAt: number; confirmToken: string } {\n  const code = String(randomInt(0, 1_000_000)).padStart(6, \"0\");\n  const confirmToken = randomBytes(24).toString(\"base64url\");\n  const expiresAt = now + CODE_TTL_SECONDS * 1000;\n  this.store.code = {\n    hash: sha256(code),\n    expiresAt,\n    attempts: 0,\n    confirmHash: sha256(confirmToken),\n  };\n  this.persist();\n  return { code, expiresAt, confirmToken };\n}\n```\nNote: `confirmToken` uses `randomBytes(24).toString(\"base64url\")` → 32 chars, high entropy. Stored as sha256. ✓ \"不进日志\" — I never log it. ✓.\n\nNow `pairTwoStepEnabled`:\n```ts\nexport function pairTwoStepEnabled(env: NodeJS.ProcessEnv = process.env): boolean {\n  const raw = (env.PAIR_TWO_STEP ?? \"\").trim().toLowerCase();\n  if (!raw) return true;\n  return raw !== \"false\" && raw !== \"0\" && raw !== \"off\";\n}\n```\n\nAnd `issueDevice`:\n```ts\nprivate issueDevice(deviceName: string, now: number): RedeemResult {\n  const deviceToken = randomBytes(32).toString(\"base64url\");\n  const tokenHash = sha256(deviceToken);\n  const id = randomBytes(8).toString(\"hex\");\n  const device: StoredDevice = {\n    id,\n    name: deviceName.trim().slice(0, 40) || \"手机\",\n    tokenHash,\n    createdAt: now,\n    ...(deviceFingerprintEnabled() ? { fingerprint: deviceFingerprint(id, tokenHash) } : {}),\n  };\n  const current = this.store.code!;\n  current.usedAt = now;\n  this.store.devices = [...this.store.devices, device]\n    .filter((item) => !item.revokedAt)\n    .sort((a, b) => (b.lastSeenAt ?? b.createdAt) - (a.lastSeenAt ?? a.createdAt))\n    .slice(0, MAX_DEVICES);\n  this.persist();\n  return {\n    deviceToken,\n    deviceId: device.id,\n    ...(device.fingerprint ? { fingerprint: device.fingerprint } : {}),\n  };\n}\n```\n\nHmm — `this.store.code!` non-null assertion. The callers (redeem/confirm) have already validated `current` exists. But to be safe, let me pass the code record or guard. Actually — `issueDevice` assumes `this.store.code` exists (both callers validated). Let me use `this.store.code` directly with a check: `if (this.store.code) this.store.code.usedAt = now;`. Cleaner — avoid `!`. Let me do that.\n\nActually, let me reconsider — to preserve `redeem` behavior BYTE-for-BYTE, let me extract VERY carefully. The original `redeem` sets `current.usedAt = now` where `current = this.store.code` (captured at function start). In `issueDevice`, `this.store.code` is the same object. Fine.\n\nOK. Now — will the refactor break existing pairing.test.ts `pairOne`? `pairOne` uses `issueCode()` + `redeem()`. `redeem` now calls `issueDevice` → same result. ✓. And the fingerprint tests, key-change tests — all use `redeem`. Should be fine.\n\nLet me now also reconsider: the `hasLiveCode()` and `codeRemainingSeconds()` — for a two-step code (begin), `hasLiveCode()` returns true (not used, not expired, attempts < max). That's fine (debug page shows \"waiting for scan\"). OK.\n\nAlright, let me write pairing.ts now. I'll do a careful Edit. Let me compose the edits:\n\nEdit 1: Add `pairTwoStepEnabled` + `begin` + extend interfaces. Actually, let me structure:\n- Add `confirmHash?: string` to `StoredCode`.\n- Add `ConfirmError` type + `ConfirmResult` alias near `RedeemError`/`RedeemResult`.\n- Add `pairTwoStepEnabled` function near `deviceFingerprintEnabled`.\n- Add `begin()` method after `issueCode()`.\n- Add `issueDevice` private + refactor `redeem` + add `confirm`.\n\nLet me do these as separate edits. Let me start.\n\nActually — I realize I should double-check: does the task want `confirmToken` to have its OWN 5-minute TTL independent of the code's `PAIR_CODE_TTL_SECONDS`? Task 1.4: \"confirmToken 一次性、5 分钟过期、与 code 绑定\". The code TTL defaults to 300s (5 min) via `PAIR_CODE_TTL_SECONDS`. By binding confirmToken to the same record/expiresAt, it expires at 5 min by default. If someone changes `PAIR_CODE_TTL_SECONDS`, both change. I'll document \"与 code 同一记录、同一 expiresAt（默认 5 分钟），绑定即同生共死\". That satisfies \"5 分钟过期（默认）与 code 绑定\". Good. Actually — hmm, \"5 分钟过期\" might be meant as a FIXED 5 min regardless of code TTL. But binding to the code's expiry is natural and the default IS 5 min. I'll document clearly. For the unit test \"过期 → 拒绝\", I'll advance `now` past `expiresAt`. Good.\n\nLet me write the code now.\n\nActually, let me reconsider `ConfirmError` naming — I'll also think about the HTTP status mapping. Let me define:\n- `unknown_code` → 404\n- `confirm_required` → 400\n- `bad_confirm` → 400\n- `code_used` → 409\n- `code_expired` → 410\n- `too_many_attempts` → 429\n\nNow, let me write pairing.ts edits."
      }
    ],
