        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "Now I see there's an EXISTING `console.warn` for \"pin not in catalog\" (line 108). Interesting — this is a warn that's NOT injectable. My new warn should be injectable. Let me think about whether to also make the existing warn injectable — the task says \"warn 可注入以便断言\" for the NEW title/vision warn. Let me keep the existing one as console.warn (don't change unrelated behavior) but route it through `deps.warn` too? Hmm — no, keep scope tight. Actually — to be consistent, let me make BOTH warns use `deps.warn ?? console.warn`? No — that changes existing behavior slightly (but harmlessly). Actually — the task says the NEW warn should be injectable. Let me add `warn` to deps and use `(deps.warn ?? console.warn)` for BOTH warns (the existing \"not in catalog\" one and the new \"no call site\" one). That's cleaner and makes all warns testable. But it's a minor change to existing code. Hmm — AGENTS.md \"不做与本需求无关的重构\". Using `deps.warn` for the existing warn is a tiny consistency improvement but not required. Let me keep it minimal: only the NEW warn uses `deps.warn`. The existing `console.warn` stays. Actually — wait, but if a test injects `warn` and calls `auxiliaryModel(\"title\")` with a pin that's NOT in the catalog, there'd be TWO warns: one via console.warn (not in catalog) and one via deps.warn (no call site). My §3.3 test pins a VALID model (`small-model`), so no \"not in catalog\" warn. Fine.\n\nHmm — but actually, let me reconsider: to be safe and clean, let me route the existing \"not in catalog\" warn through `deps.warn ?? console.warn` as well. It's a one-line change and makes the warn fully injectable (consistent). Actually — no. Let me keep it simple and focused. The task only requires the NEW warn to be injectable. I'll use `deps.warn ?? console.warn` for the new one only. Actually — hmm, you know what, let me make both use the injectable warn — it's more consistent and the test can assert \"exactly one warn\" without the existing console.warn adding noise. But the existing warn uses console.warn directly; if I change it to `deps.warn ?? console.warn`, then in the §3.3 test (valid pin), it won't fire anyway. So no difference. Let me just leave the existing one alone to minimize changes. Decision: only the new warn uses `deps.warn`.\n\nWait — actually, there's a subtle issue: if the new \"no call site\" warn uses `deps.warn ?? console.warn`, and the existing \"not in catalog\" uses `console.warn` directly, then in production both go to console.warn. Fine.\n\nLet me now compose the edits:\n\n1. Update `AuxiliaryDeps`:\n```ts\nexport interface AuxiliaryDeps {\n\tenv?: NodeJS.ProcessEnv;\n\t/** 当前会话模型；不传就读 `readLlmConfig()`（拿不到 = 没有可用模型） */\n\tcurrent?: ModelRef | null;\n\tmodels?: AuxModelLookup;\n\t/** 注入 warn 以便单测断言（2026-11-10 批 28 §三）；缺省 console.warn。 */\n\twarn?: (message: string) => void;\n\t/** 注入\"已告警用途\"集合以便单测隔离；缺省进程内单例（每个用途只告警一次）。 */\n\twarned?: Set<AuxUse>;\n}\n```\n\n2. In `auxiliaryModel`, after `const env = deps.env ?? process.env;`, add the no-call-site warn:\n```ts\n\t// 无调用点用途：调用即提示\"配了也不会生效\"，进程内只一次（见 NO_CALL_SITE_USES）。\n\t// 仍照常返回解析结果——不因为\"没接线\"就改变模型解析契约（配了返回配置值）。\n\tif (NO_CALL_SITE_USES.has(use)) {\n\t\tconst warned = deps.warned ?? warnedNoCallSite;\n\t\tif (!warned.has(use)) {\n\t\t\twarned.add(use);\n\t\t\t(deps.warn ?? console.warn)(\n\t\t\t\t`[aux] ${use} 用途当前无调用方，AUX_MODEL_${use.toUpperCase()} 配置不会生效`,\n\t\t\t);\n\t\t}\n\t}\n```\n\nWait — placement: should this be BEFORE `const current = ...` and `if (!current) return null;`? Let me place it right after `const env`. That means it fires even when `current` is null. That's \"调用时\" (on call). Good.\n\nHmm — but wait, there's a concern: the existing test `\"没有当前模型 → null\"` uses `auxiliaryModel(\"extract\", {current: null, env: {}})` — `extract` is NOT in NO_CALL_SITE_USES, so no warn. Good. And no other existing test calls `auxiliaryModel(\"title\", {current: null})`. Fine.\n\nBut — hmm, there's a subtle issue with the module-level `warnedNoCallSite` set and the existing test `\"pin 只在别的供应商里有 → 用那个供应商\"` which calls `auxiliaryModel(\"title\", ...)`. This will trigger `console.warn` once (module set). That prints a line during tests. Acceptable but noisy. And it consumes the \"once\" for `title` in the module set — but my new test injects `warned: new Set()` so it's isolated. Good.\n\nLet me make the edits."
