        "text": "Now — I realize there's a potential issue with the existing test `\"pin 只在别的供应商里有 → 用那个供应商\"` which calls `auxiliaryModel(\"title\", {current, env: {AUX_MODEL_TITLE:\"tiny-model\"}, models})`. With my change, it triggers a `console.warn` (no `warn`/`warned` injected → uses module set + console.warn). That's fine (test doesn't assert warn). But it consumes the module-level `warnedNoCallSite` for `title`. My new tests inject their own `warned` sets, so they're isolated. Good.\n\nBut — wait, there's another concern: `auxiliaryModel(\"title\", ...)` in existing tests will call `console.warn` which prints to stderr during `pnpm test`. That's noise but harmless. Actually — hmm, let me reconsider: is there a test that captures console.warn and asserts NO warns? Let me check. Probably not. Let me not worry.\n\nActually — hold on. Let me reconsider the \"只一次\" semantics once more. The task says \"调用时打一条 warn（只一次）\". My implementation dedupes per-use per-process (module set) or per injected set. That's \"只一次\". Good.\n\nNow — let me run a quick typecheck to catch issues early before doing the frontend (which is the biggest chunk). Actually, let me run typecheck now to validate the TS changes so far. Let me also run the specific unit tests. Let me do typecheck first.\n\nActually — let me reconsider: I haven't done the http probe edits yet, or the docs, or the frontend. Let me run typecheck now to catch TS errors early (cheap-ish). Let me do that.\n\nActually, let me first double-check one thing: in index.ts, `searchSessions(await getHarness(), parsed.query, parsed.options)` — `getHarness()` returns `Promise<Harness>`. Is `Harness` assignable to `SessionReader`? `SessionReader.snapshot(doc, ctx)` and `.conversation(id, ctx)`. `Harness` from pi-durable — in lifecycle.ts it's used as `searchSessions(harness, ...)`. So it should be assignable. But TS might complain if `Harness.snapshot`/`conversation` signatures differ slightly. Since lifecycle.ts:477 compiles (presumably), it's fine. Let me verify with typecheck.\n\nAlso — `Awaited<ReturnType<typeof readTranscript>>` — `readTranscript` is `async`, so `ReturnType` = `Promise<TranscriptMessage[]>`, `Awaited` = `TranscriptMessage[]`. Good.\n\nLet me run typecheck now."
