all tests in the file (and potentially across test files if run in the same process). In `pnpm --filter @lifediary/server test`, all test files run in ONE process? Let me check — `tsx --test <files>` runs each file... Actually node --test with multiple files may run them in separate processes (isolated) or same. If same process, the module state is shared. But my new tests inject their own `warned` sets, so they're isolated regardless. And the existing tests that call `auxiliaryModel(\"title\")` consume the module set's \"once\" for `title` — but that's fine (they don't assert). OK.\n\nNow — the `[aux] AUX_MODEL_EXTRACT=no-such-model 不在模型目录里` warn is from the EXISTING test `\"pin 不在目录里 → 回落当前模型\"`. That's pre-existing. Fine.\n\nOK. Now let me move to the FRONTEND (§2 UI). This is the biggest chunk. Let me design carefully.\n\nI need to:\n1. Add a \"找旧事\" entry in 设置 → 会话 (chats section).\n2. Input keyword → call `GET /api/v1/agent/sessions/search?q=&days=&limit=`.\n3. Result list → click one → use `aroundIndex` to pull context → modal (read-only, no fork).\n4. Only `web/app.js` + `web/style.css`.\n5. `node --check` (copy to .mjs).\n\nLet me design the UI:\n- In the \"会话\" settings section, add a row: \"找旧事\" with a button \"查找…\" that opens a modal. Actually — the task says \"设置 → 会话（或任务中心）加一个'找旧事'入口\". Let me add a button row in the chats section.\n- The modal: \n  - An input for keyword + a \"搜索\" button (or auto-search on input with debounce).\n  - A results list (hits). Each shows title + time + snippet (escaped, with the query highlighted? optional).\n  - Clicking a hit → fetch `GET /api/v1/agent/chat/:id/context?aroundIndex=<hit.aroundIndex>&radius=5` → show the context messages in a read-only viewer (within the same modal or a second view).\n  - Read-only: no fork, no send. Just display messages with role/time/text.\n\nLet me think about implementation approach. The modal uses `openModal(title, build, {className})` where `build(body)` fills `el.modalBody`. I'll build the DOM via `innerHTML` (with `esc()` for untrusted text) + event listeners.\n\nLet me design a self-contained function `openRecallModal()`:\n```js\nfunction openRecallModal() {\n  openModal(\"找旧事\", (body) => {\n    body.innerHTML = `\n      <p class=\"modal-desc\">在所有旧会话的原文里找一句话，点一条看前后文（只读，不会改动或新开会话）。</p>\n      <div class=\"recall-search\">\n        <input class=\"chat-search\" id=\"recall-q\" type=\"search\" placeholder=\"输入关键词，至少 2 个字\" aria-label=\"找旧事关键词\" />\n        <button class=\"btn-primary\" type=\"button\" id=\"recall-go\">查找</button>\n      </div>\n      <div id=\"recall-results\" class=\"recall-results\"><div class=\"set-hint\">输入关键词开始查找。</div></div>\n      <div id=\"recall-context\" class=\"recall-context\" hidden></div>\n    `;\n    // wire search + result click\n    ...\n  }, { className: \"modal-wide\" });\n}\n```\n\nHmm — `modal-wide` class. Let me check the CSS for `.modal-wide` and `.modal-desc`, `.set-hint`, `.chat-search`, `.btn-primary`. These exist (used elsewhere). Let me use them plus add a few new classes for recall-specific layout in style.css.\n\nFor the search:\n```js\nconst doSearch = async () => {\n  const q = input.value.trim();\n  if (q.length < 2) { results.innerHTML = `<div class=\"set-hint\">至少 2 个字。</div>`; return; }\n  results.innerHTML = `<div class=\"set-hint\">查找中…</div>`;\n  try {\n    const resp = await request(`/api/v1/agent/sessions/search?q=${encodeURIComponent(q)}&days=365&limit=20`, { cache: \"no-store\" });\n    if (!resp.ok) { ... show error ... return; }\n    const data = await resp.json();\n    const hits = data.hits || [];\n    if (!hits.length) { results.innerHTML = `<div class=\"set-hint\">没有找到相关的旧事。</div>`; return; }\n    results.replaceChildren();\n    for (const hit of hits) {\n      const row = document.createElement(\"button\");\n      row.type = \"button\";\n      row.className = \"recall-hit\";\n      row.innerHTML = `\n        <div class=\"recall-hit-head\"><span class=\"recall-hit-title\">${esc(hit.title || \"（无标题）\")}</span>\n        <span class=\"recall-hit-time\">${esc(new Date(hit.at).toLocaleString(\"zh-CN\"))}</span></div>\n        <div class=\"recall-hit-snippet\">${esc(hit.snippet)}</div>\n      `;\n      row.addEventListener(\"click\", () => void showRecallContext(hit));\n      results.append(row);\n    }\n  } catch (error) {\n    results.innerHTML = `<div class=\"set-hint\">查找失败：${esc(error.message)}</div>`;\n  }\n};\n```\n\nWait — `esc()` helper. Let me confirm it exists and its behavior. I saw `esc(...)` used in app.js (e.g., line 10156 `esc(hit.hint)`). Let me check its definition.\n\nFor `showRecallContext(hit)`:\n```js\nconst showRecallContext = async (hit) => {\n  const box = document.getElementById(\"recall-context\");\n  box.hidden = false;\n  box.innerHTML = `<div class=\"set-hint\">读取上下文…</div>`;\n  try {\n    const resp = await request(`/api/v1/agent/chat/${encodeURIComponent(hit.conversationId)}/context?aroundIndex=${hit.aroundIndex}&radius=5`, { cache: \"no-store\" });\n    if (!resp.ok) { box.innerHTML = `<div class=\"set-hint\">读不到上下文（${resp.status}）。</div>`; return; }\n    const data = await resp.json();\n    // data.messages: [{role, text, at, index}]\n    ...render read-only messages...\n  } catch (error) { ... }\n};\n```\n\nLet me think about the context viewer:\n- Header: \"会话：title · 共 total 条 · 显示 from–to\" + a \"返回列表\" button.\n- Messages: each with role (我/Selenite), time, text. Highlight the message at `index === hit.aroundIndex`.\n- Read-only: no input, no fork, no send buttons.\n\nLet me render:\n```js\nconst head = document.createElement(\"div\");\nhead.className = \"recall-ctx-head\";\nhead.innerHTML = `<button class=\"ghost\" type=\"button\" id=\"recall-back\">← 返回结果</button>\n  <span class=\"recall-ctx-meta\">${esc(hit.title || \"会话\")} · 共 ${data.total} 条 · 第 ${data.from}–${data.to} 条</span>`;\nbox.replaceChildren(head);\nfor (const msg of data.messages || []) {\n  const line = document.createElement(\"div\");\n  line.className = `recall-msg ${msg.role === \"user\" ? \"recall-msg-user\" : \"recall-msg-assistant\"}${msg.index === hit.aroundIndex ? \" recall-msg-hit\" : \"\"}`;\n  line.innerHTML = `<div class=\"recall-msg-meta\">${msg.role === \"user\" ? \"我\" : \"Selenite\"} · ${esc(new Date(msg.at).toLocaleString(\"zh-CN\"))} · #${msg.index}</div>\n    <div class=\"recall-msg-text\">${esc(msg.text || \"（空）\")}</div>`;\n  box.append(line);\n}\nhead.querySelector(\"#recall-back\").addEventListener(\"click\", () => { box.hidden = true; box.replaceChildren(); });\n```\n\nNote: `data.messages` could contain HTML-unsafe text → use `esc()`. Good. Also — `msg.text` might contain markdown; I'll just show plain text (esc'd). Fine.\n\nNow — where to add the \"找旧事\" entry? In the chats settings section. Let me add a row in the `card` near \"搜索会话\". Actually — the task says \"设置 → 会话（或任务中心）加一个'找旧事'入口\". Let me add a row with a button \"找旧事\" that opens the modal. Let me add it right after the \"搜索会话\" row (or after the search results blocks). Let me put it near the top of the 会话 card. Actually — let me add it as a new row after \"搜索会话\" block but the search results divs are dynamic. Let me add a dedicated row near the top.\n\nHmm — let me reconsider. The \"会话\" settings card currently has:\n- \"搜索会话\" row (input) + search-results + content-results\n- divider + \"回车发送\" switch\n- divider + \"工具活动\" switch\n- divider + \"已移除的会话\" (conditional)\n- divider + \"导出全部数据\"\n\nI'll add a \"找旧事\" row after the content-results block (before the \"回车发送\" divider). Let me add:\n```\n${rowMarkup(\n  \"找旧事\",\n  \"在所有旧会话的原文里搜一句话，点结果看前后文（只读，不新开会话）\",\n  `<button class=\"ghost\" type=\"button\" id=\"open-recall\">查找…</button>`,\n)}\n<div class=\"divider\"></div>\n```\nAnd wire `document.getElementById(\"open-recall\")?.addEventListener(\"click\", () => openRecallModal());`.\n\nNow the helper functions `esc`, `request`, `openModal`, `closeModal` are all available. Let me verify `esc` exists.\n\nLet me