        "text": "I'll add `PAIR_TWO_STEP: \"false\"` to line 2811's startServer call. But wait — §30 is the LAST test. And I want to add §31 (two-step) which needs `PAIR_TWO_STEP=true`. Let me restructure:\n\nOption A: Add `PAIR_TWO_STEP: \"false\"` to line 2811 (so §30 works). Then for §31, restart the server with `PAIR_TWO_STEP: \"true\"` and a separate pairing store path. Then §31 tests. Then finally cleanup.\n\nActually — let me reconsider: maybe simpler to run §31 FIRST with a dedicated server (PAIR_TWO_STEP=true), then §30 with PAIR_TWO_STEP=false. But §30 currently is at the end. Let me insert §31 AFTER §30 but with a server restart.\n\nLet me structure:\n- Line 2811: add `PAIR_TWO_STEP: \"false\"` → §30 works with old single-stage.\n- After §30 (line 2854), insert §31: kill server, restart with `PAIR_TWO_STEP: \"true\"` + separate `PAIRING_STORE_PATH`, then test begin/confirm/redeem-gated/sessions-search.\n\nWait — but §31 with `PAIR_TWO_STEP=true` — the `redeem` endpoint returns 410. And `begin`/`confirm` are active. Good.\n\nAlso — for §31's `sessions/search` test: `GET /api/v1/agent/sessions/search?q=` → 400 (empty), `?q=爬` → 400, `?q=不存在的词xyz` → 200 `{hits:[]}`. These don't need real sessions. But `searchSessions(await getHarness(), ...)` — will `getHarness()` work in the probe (faux provider)? It should. Let me test. Actually — there's a risk `getHarness()` throws if no model config. Let me check: in the probe, `LLM_PROVIDER=faux`, `LLM_API_KEY=\"\"`. Is there a `readLlmConfig()`? The `/api/v1/agent/search` endpoint checks `readLlmConfig()` and returns `{hits:[]}` if null. Hmm. But `searchSessions` uses `getHarness()` directly (no LLM config check). If `getHarness()` requires a model config, it might fail.\n\nLet me check `Harness.open` in lifecycle.ts line 1118 — I can read it (just not edit). Let me check. Actually — let me think: the `recall_sessions` tool is wired into `createTools` and uses `getHarness()`. If `getHarness()` fails without config, the tool would fail too (it has try/catch). In the probe with faux, there IS a model config (faux model). So `getHarness()` works. Let me just try it in the probe and see. Actually — to be safe, let me make the §31 sessions/search test handle a possible 500 gracefully? No — that would hide a real failure. Let me first VERIFY by running the http probe after adding the tests. If `getHarness()` fails, I'll add a guard to my endpoint (e.g., wrap in try/catch → return `{hits:[]}` or check `readLlmConfig()`).\n\nHmm — actually, let me reconsider: my endpoint calls `searchSessions(await getHarness(), ...)`. If `getHarness()` rejects, `app.onError` → 500. In the probe, that would fail my §31 test. Let me proactively add a `readLlmConfig()` check to the endpoint? Actually — `searchTranscripts` (the existing `/agent/search`) checks `if (!readLlmConfig()) return c.json({ hits: [] });`. For consistency, maybe my endpoint should too. But `searchSessions` reads durable directly (doesn't need a model). Hmm. But `getHarness()` might need a model config to open. Let me check `Harness.open` quickly.\n\nLet me read lifecycle.ts around 1118 (read only, allowed)."
